1
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:28,359
Let's do some training before
going to Akhisar, shall we?

2
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:36,319
You will fight against both
of us alone, father, right?

3
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:39,399
That might be a
bit difficult for you.

4
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:46,759
It is not the number of men
that brings victory in battle.

5
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:51,519
It is the courage that
brings victory in war, sons.

6
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,119
Make your move.

7
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:15,919
Are Alps ready for the conquest?

8
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:18,919
We are always ready, my
Bey. We are strong and brave.

9
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:35,639
You are fast.

10
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:37,519
But not enough for me.

11
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:47,479
-Alaeddin.
-My Bey.

12
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:52,959
Tell me, how are you
going to attack the castle?

13
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:55,279
We will hit from the left wing, my Bey.

14
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:59,519
And also from the right wing, my Bey.

15
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:11,999
We will attack from all fronts and
bring Akhisar down just like this, my Bey.

16
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:15,159
What if another unit comes from behind?

17
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,798
What will you do then?

18
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,918
Brother, behind you

19
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:28,159
We always have a watchman behind us, my Bey.

20
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:29,639
Don't worry.

21
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:46,279
Father... Don't father.

22
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:47,719
Don't hurt my brothers..

23
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:54,279
You three think you are
equal to us if you gather, huh?

24
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:57,319
It's not that easy.
-Don't..

25
00:04:57,720 --> 00:04:59,519
Don't, father, don't hurt them.

26
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:02,559
Look at me.

27
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:03,879
You are cheating.

28
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:06,519
You know my weak spot well.

29
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:10,119
They should pray for you. You.

30
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:20,479
Bala.

31
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:24,239
Come here.

32
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:35,279
My family could have been by my side too.

33
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:40,439
My mother, father, maybe my siblings.

34
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:45,599
You took them all from me.

35
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:57,759
Meryem.

36
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:06,879
What are you doing here? -I...

37
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:12,439
...saw you coming to the cemetery
alone, so I didn't want to leave you alone.

38
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:16,879
Besides, I am considered
one of the Sisters now, right?

39
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:19,279
Yes. Right.

40
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:22,439
Who is it?

41
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:28,599
She is my little girl who will never grow up.

42
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:33,639
Children are like embroidery, Meryem daughter.

43
00:06:33,880 --> 00:06:36,879
Even if they are gone,
their mark always remains.

44
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:38,679
A family is the same.

45
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:41,559
The pain of their absence is big.

46
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:45,079
But this pain keeps me standing.

47
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:46,879
The loss of a child or..

48
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:49,279
..the loss of a mother..

49
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:53,079
...hurts people from the same place.

50
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:56,879
But anger and hatred...

51
00:06:58,080 --> 00:06:59,239
...burn your heart.

52
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:02,879
They leave you in the dark, Meryem daughter.

53
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:07,519
I won't find peace without
taking revenge on those infidels...

54
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:10,719
...who took my
family, Bala Hatun.

55
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:14,279
This revenge keeps me alive.

56
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:18,839
-If you allow me.
-Meryem.

57
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:23,359
I really like you, Meryem.

58
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:26,439
You remind me of my youth.

59
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:32,519
I'm glad you met Fatma.

60
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:34,119
I'm glad you came to our tribe.

61
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,879
God has shown His justice.

62
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:43,439
You took my mother...

63
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:46,119
...and He took your daughter.

64
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:50,959
I long for you in such a
way that my daughter....

65
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:53,759
...I look for you in every new face I see.

66
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:03,239
I will make you pay for
all the suffering I endured.

67
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:06,119
My Bey.

68
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:08,759
The council is ready, they are waiting for you.

69
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:11,319
Orhan, Alaeddin. You go on.

70
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:13,999
Come on, my daughter.

71
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:21,239
Meryem.

72
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:24,119
Bring some sherbet, my daughter.

73
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:25,759
Sure, Bala Hatun.

74
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:29,159
Drink some sherbet before
going to the council, my Bey.

75
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:31,599
So you care for your husband, huh?

76
00:08:32,039 --> 00:08:35,639
You are my only one, Kara
Osman. Who else would I care for?

77
00:08:45,560 --> 00:08:48,199
So you are the Meryem..

78
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:51,439
...Fatma talks about all the time.

79
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:54,559
It's an honor to meet you, Osman Bey.

80
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:08,159
Let me help you.

81
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:16,799
I am sorry.

82
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:19,319
I got excited.

83
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:23,239
It's okay. Take this.

84
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:27,519
So, tell me.

85
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:29,799
Are you from nearby tribes?

86
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:31,919
Do we know your family? Your father?

87
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:36,519
We are nomads.

88
00:09:36,920 --> 00:09:38,399
We just arrived here.

89
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:44,799
They killed my mother and
father when I was little, Osman Bey.

90
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:49,639
Meryem will join the Sisters, my Bey.

91
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:54,439
She is being trained.

92
00:09:55,040 --> 00:09:56,879
So, you will become a Sister, huh?

93
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:58,879
You are brave.

94
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:03,479
The courage of your heart shines in your eyes.

95
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:09,199
I will do everything I can to take
revenge for my family, Osman Bey.

96
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:20,079
The path of the Sisters and
ours is not the path of revenge.

97
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:25,239
Our path is the path of justice.

98
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:32,119
The scales of justice must be set with patience.

99
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:37,679
Otherwise, we will become oppressors.

100
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,359
Yes, Osman Bey.

101
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:43,479
Go now.

102
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:46,599
Thank you my daughter, thank you.

103
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:50,999
Bala, I am going to see the Beys.

104
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:05,279
The man who took my family and my childhood.

105
00:11:07,680 --> 00:11:12,239
But how can I be so weak
when I am close to them?

106
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:18,599
God, let me be strong.

107
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:13,279
Alps! Someone's coming

108
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:18,079
Stop!

109
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:23,399
You are on the border of Kayi. Who are you?

110
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:29,799
I am the envoy of the glorious
Mongol State's Head Commander...

111
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:31,719
...who makes everyone kneel...

112
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:34,839
...and who brings an order to the world...

113
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:38,839
...Ulugan.
What are you doing here?

114
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:41,959
We are here to demand
your Osman Bey's allegiance...

115
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:44,599
...and collect the tribute we imposed on him.

116
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:50,319
If you stand in our way, your
fate will be the same as these fools.

117
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:55,959
If you don't want to be dragged
behind my horse, step aside.

118
00:12:58,040 --> 00:13:02,879
We won't let you cross our border
with the corpses you drag behind you.

119
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:04,799
We will inform Osman Bey!

120
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:07,999
I will go there however I want.

121
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,639
-Neither you nor Osman can stop this.
-Alps!

122
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:12,559
Attack!

123
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:31,439
The fate of those who stand
against the Mongols is death.

124
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:33,409
Nokers(Mongolian Soldiers)!

125
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:36,479
We are going to Osman's tribe. Come on!

126
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:46,079
Blood! Blood! Blood!

127
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:47,399
Blood! Blood! Blood!

128
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:52,279
Blood! Blood! Blood!

129
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:54,839
Saruca Bey.

130
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:59,119
Your father Bayhan Bey...

131
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:04,479
...sacrificed his life for his state
and nation without hesitating.

132
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:10,359
Now his property and his cause are yours now.

133
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:16,519
Beylic of Kizilcinarogullari will be ruled...

134
00:14:17,760 --> 00:14:19,919
...by you, Saruca Bey.

135
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:24,799
May Allah keep you on the right path.

136
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:26,239
Aameen, my Bey.

137
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:31,759
The right path is your path, my Bey.

138
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:35,719
May Allah give you a long life.

139
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:39,039
Thank you, thank you.
I appreciate it.

140
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:45,759
Beys, Karesi Bey...

141
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:50,188
...who supported heathens
all the time with your help

142
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:53,519
as well and valued his
interest above anything else...

143
00:14:54,680 --> 00:14:59,479
...has lost his reputation and
also the chance to stop us.

144
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:01,519
Thanks to Allah, my Bey.

145
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:06,879
From now on, we will discuss
our new target and what to do.

146
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:13,319
At dawn, we will reach Akhisar
and start hitting the walls.

147
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:15,959
Okay, my Bey.
Okay, my Bey.

148
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:19,799
My Bey.

149
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:23,719
Akhisar is a nest of heathens with solid walls.

150
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:27,519
Can we destroy them by shooting with catapults?

151
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:32,719
Begum Hatun, you mus be thinking...

152
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:37,719
...alps will fall weak and impatient...

153
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:42,199
..if the siege of Akhisar takes
longer than expected, right?

154
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:44,479
Remember this.

155
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:49,919
Our hearts burning to
bring justice in those lands...

156
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:54,679
...are stronger than their walls
inside which they hide their oppression.

157
00:15:56,640 --> 00:16:00,759
Lukas and Sofia will see that too.

158
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:06,159
Listen to me carefully now.

159
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:10,719
Cerkutay. Boran.

160
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:15,159
You two will be in the front line with me.

161
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:18,439
Orhan and Alaaddin.

162
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:21,679
You will be in the left wing.

163
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:26,279
Begum Hatun.

164
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:28,679
And Saruca.

165
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:35,599
You two will be in the right wing.

166
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:38,959
-As you order, my Bey.
-I want no mistakes.

167
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:41,319
We'll never fall into despair.

168
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:45,007
Until the call of Muhammad
is recited in the square...

169
00:16:45,019 --> 00:16:48,279
...of Akhisar and the flag
of Kayi raises on the walls,

170
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:49,879
...we'll never stop.

171
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,919
God willing

172
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:04,439
Hurry up, hurry up.

173
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:08,159
-Faster.
-Go over there.

174
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:11,479
Commander Lukas.

175
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:15,159
A message from our scouts.

176
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:17,799
Osman completed his preparations secretly.

177
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:20,919
Come here, Osman.

178
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:22,759
Come.

179
00:17:24,280 --> 00:17:27,637
There should be no holes in the walls!

180
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:30,639
Repair them all.

181
00:17:34,160 --> 00:17:37,959
Take the long-ranged bows up on the walls.

182
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:40,879
Take the Greek fire with you.

183
00:17:43,120 --> 00:17:47,719
I'm forbidding you to use sleep...

184
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:50,719
...and even rest till this battle ends!

185
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:53,839
Is that clear?

186
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:57,599
-Yes, commander!
-Hristo, guide them.

187
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:01,319
Soldiers, come on

188
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:08,879
Karesi turned out to be an old coward, huh?

189
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:13,839
He couldn't stand against
Osman but just ran away.

190
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:16,319
We will stand, Sofia.

191
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:19,999
We won't give Osman even a single fortress.

192
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:25,199
Any news from Lord of Iznik?

193
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:28,119
Are the reinforcements coming?

194
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:30,439
Don't worry.

195
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:34,119
When Osman attacks our walls

196
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:38,679
...we'll hit him from
somewhere he never expects.

197
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:42,599
In the back.

198
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:54,439
He thinks he can beat me,
my Shahzade(Prince).

199
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:57,719
What now? What?

200
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:03,599
What is this? Are you ripping Ghazi in two?

201
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:10,159
We haven't eaten all
together for long. Right, Ghazi?

202
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:13,239
Right. You never stop fighting, my Bey.

203
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:16,159
You take my father with you as well.

204
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:19,279
Are you complaining, Ghazi Alp?

205
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:20,919
No, Boran Bey.

206
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:25,079
But everybody goes to the fight
and I stay with hatuns in the tribe.

207
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:29,799
You should be strong enough
to carry steel swords first.

208
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:32,599
Your father is right, Ghazi.

209
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:36,799
-There is still time for that.
-The matter between you and me is settled.

210
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:39,319
Don't mess with me anymore,
tall Shahzade(Prince).

211
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:42,119
-Right, Gonca Hatun?
-Yes.

212
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:43,599
Ghazi Alp is right.

213
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:45,839
Don't mess with him,
Tall Shahzade(Prince).

214
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:51,279
Alright then. Let's eat all together.

215
00:19:56,280 --> 00:19:58,159
Let's eat.

216
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:03,799
Meryem.

217
00:20:07,520 --> 00:20:10,199
Join the table, girl. Eat.

218
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:12,719
I don't want to disturb, my Bey.

219
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:15,039
You won't be disturbing anyone.

220
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:19,199
Take a seat, girl.

221
00:20:22,360 --> 00:20:25,639
Everybody in the tribe
has a place in this table.

222
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:30,759
If you don't take me to the
fight, I will go myself, father.

223
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:32,879
Behave.

224
00:20:33,520 --> 00:20:34,759
Sister.

225
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:39,759
Do Ghazi's words remind you something?

226
00:20:40,880 --> 00:20:44,319
-Ha? Ha, my Bey?
-Yes, yes.

227
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:49,359
But it wasn't a good incident.

228
00:20:50,440 --> 00:20:52,879
-Right, Fatma?
-Father...

229
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:54,799
Don't.

230
00:20:58,400 --> 00:21:01,239
Don't tell, please.

231
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:03,479
Tell, Alaaddin.

232
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:05,079
Alright, my Bey.

233
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:07,079
Ghazi.

234
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:09,879
At your age

235
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:11,919
...Fatma insisted on fighting.

236
00:21:12,640 --> 00:21:13,719
Then...

237
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:16,639
One day, our sister was...

238
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:19,119
What sister?

239
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:33,679
Come here, Halime.

240
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:44,039
Oh, I know her!
-No!

241
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:50,999
So... did she go?

242
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,359
Of course she did

243
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,919
She hid in the cart.

244
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:58,879
And fell into the battlefield all of a sudden

245
00:21:59,320 --> 00:22:02,839
And when she came back

246
00:22:03,680 --> 00:22:05,399
You won't believe this!

247
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:10,359
She kept saying "I should
have never gone there, my Bey!"

248
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:13,919
"It was too early for me." Right, Fatma?

249
00:22:14,760 --> 00:22:15,879
Father.

250
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:19,639
How could you tell Ghazi about this?

251
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:24,839
He'll talk about it for days.
I should tell him, of course.

252
00:22:25,440 --> 00:22:27,999
Actually, you know what she did?

253
00:22:28,320 --> 00:22:31,839
She also attempted to take
her deceased sister with her

254
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:34,199
..but her mother didn't let.

255
00:22:36,960 --> 00:22:41,279
Oh Fatma... You gave us a rough time.

256
00:22:48,280 --> 00:22:51,299
I will bring some halvah(a type of dessert).

257
00:22:54,840 --> 00:22:59,719
You know what, my Bey? Holofira
should say a table prayer for us.

258
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:04,879
Well...

259
00:23:06,080 --> 00:23:11,639
Mother, your son is making fun of
me as I can't say the words correctly.

260
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:15,599
-Orhan...
-Mother... My Bey, I was...

261
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:20,839
It was just a joke... I'm sorry.

262
00:23:22,520 --> 00:23:24,599
Well...

263
00:23:25,160 --> 00:23:29,639
Meryem, how is your training with Sisters going

264
00:23:29,800 --> 00:23:32,999
Thankfully, Fatma
Hatun takes care of me.

265
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:35,279
But I'm a slow learner.

266
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:37,679
Don't mind what she says, father.

267
00:23:37,840 --> 00:23:39,679
She holds the sword strongly.

268
00:23:39,720 --> 00:23:41,759
And she's a quick learner.

269
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:45,999
The trainings will make you stronger.

270
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:50,079
Your patience too. And..

271
00:23:50,840 --> 00:23:53,479
And they will restrain your anger.

272
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:58,719
Here we go.

273
00:23:59,120 --> 00:24:02,469
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate. You may start.

274
00:24:02,920 --> 00:24:04,639
Enjoy the meals.

275
00:24:10,720 --> 00:24:12,919
Thanks to Allah

276
00:24:13,240 --> 00:24:15,559
...my father is combing my hair again.

277
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:19,599
I feel scared whenever you go on a duty.

278
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:24,319
-Thinking you may not come back.
-No, I don't believe that.

279
00:24:25,960 --> 00:24:27,639
My pretty daughter...

280
00:24:27,760 --> 00:24:30,399
My little gazelle is afraid of nothing at all.

281
00:24:30,560 --> 00:24:32,679
I'm a little wolf, though.

282
00:24:33,080 --> 00:24:35,759
A little wolf from the lineage of Kayis.

283
00:24:35,760 --> 00:24:38,239
Look at this little wolf!

284
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:47,759
Father, when will we talk to Osman Bey?

285
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:51,159
When will we tell him we are Kayi as well.

286
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:53,959
Kayi?

287
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:58,999
Will we keep hiding the fact that
your grandfather is Sungur Tegin?

288
00:25:05,120 --> 00:25:06,519
My pretty girl.

289
00:25:07,320 --> 00:25:09,319
We already talked about this.

290
00:25:09,560 --> 00:25:13,519
Never talk about this before I
mention this subject, alright?

291
00:25:20,120 --> 00:25:22,159
Can I come in?

292
00:25:29,920 --> 00:25:31,679
You can, Begum Hatun.

293
00:25:40,040 --> 00:25:43,279
I couldn't find any time
to thank you earlier, Ilbay.

294
00:25:43,600 --> 00:25:47,519
I still remember that I got out of
Karesi's dungeon thanks to you.

295
00:25:49,120 --> 00:25:50,769
Don't even mention it.

296
00:25:50,840 --> 00:25:53,959
Osman Bey gave me a duty and I carried it out.

297
00:25:54,080 --> 00:25:55,599
Fine.

298
00:25:55,920 --> 00:25:57,839
Still, I owe you one.

299
00:25:58,280 --> 00:25:59,719
Thank you.

300
00:26:06,560 --> 00:26:08,559
My father saves everyone.

301
00:26:08,600 --> 00:26:11,239
When I get older,
I will be like him.

302
00:26:12,040 --> 00:26:13,999
I can see that.

303
00:26:14,640 --> 00:26:18,119
You are brave like your father.

304
00:26:22,560 --> 00:26:24,919
You will be a tough woman.

305
00:26:32,720 --> 00:26:35,239
I want to give you this mirror as a gift.

306
00:26:45,400 --> 00:26:49,679
Through it, you can see how
much you take after your father.

307
00:26:50,640 --> 00:26:53,719
Thanks, Begum Hatun. This is beautiful.

308
00:27:01,840 --> 00:27:04,639
Thank you, Begum Hatun.
Thank you.

309
00:27:10,120 --> 00:27:13,799
I haven't seen her so happy for long.

310
00:27:15,200 --> 00:27:17,359
But why did you?

311
00:27:18,040 --> 00:27:20,599
I didn't help you hoping something in return.

312
00:27:21,160 --> 00:27:24,439
I didn't give her that in return for the favor.

313
00:27:26,120 --> 00:27:28,479
It's been Ayse Hatun and me.

314
00:27:41,640 --> 00:27:45,159
Well... I should go now.

315
00:27:48,440 --> 00:27:50,079
Good night.

316
00:27:54,880 --> 00:27:56,679
Good night.

317
00:28:05,240 --> 00:28:06,879
Begum Hatun.

318
00:28:10,160 --> 00:28:11,679
Gonca.

319
00:28:12,280 --> 00:28:14,039
Welcome.

320
00:28:18,320 --> 00:28:22,279
I wanted to thank you
but I couldn't find a chance.

321
00:28:25,640 --> 00:28:27,559
No need for that.

322
00:28:28,480 --> 00:28:31,879
I have to. You protected me and my secret.

323
00:28:32,120 --> 00:28:34,199
I owe you one.

324
00:28:36,200 --> 00:28:38,239
You're wrong, Begum Hatun.

325
00:28:38,800 --> 00:28:41,959
I protect neither you nor your secret.

326
00:28:43,760 --> 00:28:45,599
If I had exposed the secret,

327
00:28:46,640 --> 00:28:49,679
...there would have been no peace here.

328
00:28:50,200 --> 00:28:52,999
If you didn't lead the troop of Kecilishah,

329
00:28:53,480 --> 00:28:55,159
...I'd have told others by now.

330
00:28:55,240 --> 00:28:59,519
Please, Gonca. I have no bad intentions.

331
00:29:00,680 --> 00:29:03,559
I just fell in love.

332
00:29:05,080 --> 00:29:06,479
And it was long before Bala.

333
00:29:08,680 --> 00:29:10,959
-You don't understand...
-Hatun!

334
00:29:12,160 --> 00:29:14,159
Do you have no shame at all?

335
00:29:14,760 --> 00:29:19,159
The man who you said
you fell in with has a wife!

336
00:29:20,960 --> 00:29:24,759
It was long before, I said. Long before.

337
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:29,439
There is no past or future for this matter.

338
00:29:30,720 --> 00:29:31,479
From now on

339
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:35,879
...you will stay away from father and mother.

340
00:29:37,080 --> 00:29:38,319
One mistake.

341
00:29:38,840 --> 00:29:41,479
If you make one mistake, Begum

342
00:29:42,600 --> 00:29:44,279
..I will expose the secret.

343
00:29:47,080 --> 00:29:49,439
And you will be a total disgrace then.

344
00:29:50,800 --> 00:29:53,759
-Gonca.
-I said my final words, Begum.

345
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:57,919
You either stay here with manners...

346
00:29:58,400 --> 00:30:02,519
...or nobody will want to ever
remember your name when you go!

347
00:30:17,080 --> 00:30:19,439
I helped you a lot...

348
00:30:19,920 --> 00:30:22,399
...and you show ingratitude in return!

349
00:30:25,360 --> 00:30:26,759
What was that?

350
00:30:29,120 --> 00:30:30,519
Sister.

351
00:30:32,680 --> 00:30:34,519
What does Gonca Hatun mean?

352
00:30:35,280 --> 00:30:37,239
Where are you going?

353
00:30:39,200 --> 00:30:41,519
Today, I've learned such a thing today...

354
00:30:42,040 --> 00:30:44,319
...that nobody can send us away.

355
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:48,679
Well... Saruca will join Osman Bey's council.

356
00:30:49,280 --> 00:30:52,599
He's got closer to Osman Bey. What will I do?

357
00:30:53,400 --> 00:30:57,359
Then... Then you should hurry up.

358
00:30:59,080 --> 00:31:01,999
Either you will be Osman Bey's son-in-law...

359
00:31:02,520 --> 00:31:05,479
Or I will..

360
00:31:09,480 --> 00:31:11,159
You will what?

361
00:31:12,960 --> 00:31:15,679
I will find a way to rule Kayis.

362
00:31:48,840 --> 00:31:53,359
Maybe save your life
during this conquest, Ilbay.

363
00:31:54,200 --> 00:31:55,879
So I will pay back.

364
00:31:56,120 --> 00:31:57,679
Don't mention it.

365
00:31:58,160 --> 00:31:59,999
You owe nothing, Begum Hatun.

366
00:32:00,120 --> 00:32:02,679
And I say I will pay.

367
00:32:25,640 --> 00:32:27,879
-Orhan.
-My Bey.

368
00:32:27,960 --> 00:32:31,919
What's the news? Are the catapults on the way?
-Yes, my Bey?

369
00:32:31,960 --> 00:32:36,719
Saruca and Yusuf are leading them. They
must be about to reach the headquarters.

370
00:32:38,320 --> 00:32:40,199
Lukas and Sofia...

371
00:32:40,840 --> 00:32:43,719
...will be trapped in Akhisar like rats today.

372
00:32:43,960 --> 00:32:47,919
Today, Akhisar will the property of Kayis.

373
00:32:50,800 --> 00:32:54,599
Our target is Akhisar!

374
00:32:54,840 --> 00:32:59,679
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!

375
00:33:00,080 --> 00:33:01,879
Let's go.

376
00:33:32,560 --> 00:33:34,079
Commander Lukas.

377
00:33:35,680 --> 00:33:37,839
Preparations are almost finished.

378
00:33:38,120 --> 00:33:40,439
We'll resist against Osman and his army.

379
00:33:40,480 --> 00:33:42,839
Any news from the troop coming from Iznik?

380
00:33:43,080 --> 00:33:45,319
They'll arrive in tomorrow morning.

381
00:33:45,480 --> 00:33:48,599
I will welcome them, Lukas.

382
00:33:50,000 --> 00:33:53,919
I know Osman's weakest spot.

383
00:33:54,800 --> 00:33:56,639
I will lead the army.

384
00:33:57,440 --> 00:34:01,239
When you attack from behind,
I will leave the fortress and hit!

385
00:34:02,160 --> 00:34:04,479
I will make them face such a defeat...

386
00:34:04,880 --> 00:34:08,199
...this field will be painted with their blood.

387
00:34:08,600 --> 00:34:12,399
Osman will never be able to
take this fortress. Don't worry.

388
00:34:14,120 --> 00:34:15,799
I have to go now.

389
00:34:16,520 --> 00:34:18,958
Where? It's too soon.

390
00:34:18,960 --> 00:34:23,799
I promised my little bird
Poena that I would meet her.

391
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:28,119
You never know, Lukas.

392
00:34:30,159 --> 00:34:33,199
We may beat Osman without fighting.

393
00:35:24,240 --> 00:35:28,359
Osman, where are you? Come out!

394
00:35:40,160 --> 00:35:41,799
Who are you?

395
00:35:42,400 --> 00:35:43,839
What's happening?

396
00:35:44,920 --> 00:35:49,039
I am the envoy of Ulugan,
commander of the glorious...

397
00:35:49,040 --> 00:35:50,919
..Mongol State.

398
00:35:51,320 --> 00:35:55,159
The Bey of your tribe, Osman,
must step forward immediately.

399
00:35:55,160 --> 00:35:57,639
Stop there, envoy. Calm down.

400
00:35:58,320 --> 00:36:00,079
Osman Bey is not here.

401
00:36:00,840 --> 00:36:04,639
Say what you have to say when
he comes. Now leave the tribe.

402
00:36:05,720 --> 00:36:07,439
Otherwise, it will not end well.

403
00:36:14,360 --> 00:36:17,599
Then, I will wait in your Bey's tent.

404
00:36:17,600 --> 00:36:19,439
You must get through me first.

405
00:36:27,840 --> 00:36:29,279
What's happening here?

406
00:36:32,760 --> 00:36:33,799
Mother...

407
00:36:34,760 --> 00:36:36,519
Mongols have no mercy.

408
00:36:36,520 --> 00:36:38,519
Why have they come now?

409
00:36:38,720 --> 00:36:41,559
We will now find out what they want, daughter.

410
00:36:43,680 --> 00:36:44,799
Turhan.

411
00:36:46,800 --> 00:36:48,119
What is happening here?

412
00:36:48,200 --> 00:36:50,519
This man is a Mongol envoy, Bala Hatun.

413
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:02,359
Let him come close.

414
00:37:03,000 --> 00:37:07,199
Since he is an envoy, he
must have something to tell us.

415
00:37:07,880 --> 00:37:13,879
Listen to the Hatun and live a
long life. Otherwise, I will crush you.

416
00:37:13,960 --> 00:37:15,119
Turhan.

417
00:37:16,120 --> 00:37:17,159
Let him.

418
00:37:31,720 --> 00:37:35,419
You did not come with
manners, but speak what you

419
00:37:35,431 --> 00:37:39,439
have to say properly, and
then leave our tribe, envoy.

420
00:38:25,520 --> 00:38:26,719
My Beys.

421
00:38:27,360 --> 00:38:28,599
My Alps.

422
00:38:28,680 --> 00:38:31,479
My lions who do not hold back from hardship...

423
00:38:31,760 --> 00:38:36,359
...who rush into battle and
martyrdom without hesitation.

424
00:38:37,360 --> 00:38:39,119
The time has come.

425
00:38:39,560 --> 00:38:46,959
Today is the day of riot. Here is Akhisar.

426
00:38:51,680 --> 00:38:52,879
And here we are.

427
00:38:54,520 --> 00:38:58,559
I swear by the faith burning
in our hearts like a fire!

428
00:38:58,560 --> 00:39:00,399
We swear!

429
00:39:03,120 --> 00:39:07,519
By the swords that cast
fear into all infidels....

430
00:39:08,840 --> 00:39:12,119
...with their gleam and
enlighten many minds, I swear!

431
00:39:12,120 --> 00:39:13,599
We swear!

432
00:39:13,600 --> 00:39:15,879
Today, we will be martyrs here.

433
00:39:15,960 --> 00:39:21,599
But we will never stop until we
make Akhisar the homeland of Turks.

434
00:39:22,130 --> 00:39:35,079
Allah is the Greatest!

435
00:39:35,080 --> 00:39:36,799
Osman..

436
00:39:40,440 --> 00:39:41,799
You..

437
00:39:43,160 --> 00:39:47,679
...and those with you, those
shouting loudly, all of you...

438
00:39:48,320 --> 00:39:52,199
I will make you cry out in
pain in the square of Akhisar.

439
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:05,519
My soldiers!

440
00:40:06,800 --> 00:40:08,799
My fearless soldiers!

441
00:40:09,560 --> 00:40:13,919
I know you are not scared of anything!

442
00:40:14,120 --> 00:40:17,359
But I see fear in some of your eyes.

443
00:40:18,960 --> 00:40:27,319
And I must say this to them, do not be deceived
by the Turks' loud noise, their best talent!

444
00:40:34,720 --> 00:40:36,279
Do you hear them?

445
00:40:37,440 --> 00:40:40,119
Do you understand what the Turks are saying?

446
00:40:40,760 --> 00:40:47,159
They claim their God is greater
than ours, greater than Jesus Christ...

447
00:40:47,160 --> 00:40:49,839
...greater than Holy Rome.

448
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:53,766
But they do not know
that we are the children

449
00:40:53,778 --> 00:40:57,639
of a civilization that
has stood for centuries.

450
00:40:58,320 --> 00:41:04,439
We are the descendants of brave
knights and ruthless legionaries.

451
00:41:04,440 --> 00:41:10,279
Even if we knew we would drown
in our own blood, we would still fight.

452
00:41:10,280 --> 00:41:12,839
We never run away from fighting.

453
00:41:13,080 --> 00:41:17,959
Glorious soldiers of the
Great Empire, now I ask you...

454
00:41:19,520 --> 00:41:26,639
These shepherds who invade your land
threaten your lives, and your religion...

455
00:41:26,640 --> 00:41:28,359
Are you afraid of them?

456
00:41:28,360 --> 00:41:30,319
No!

457
00:41:30,320 --> 00:41:31,679
Are you afraid?

458
00:41:35,600 --> 00:41:41,839
Then, until there is not
one left alive on this earth...

459
00:41:42,520 --> 00:41:51,279
Death to the Turks!

460
00:41:55,040 --> 00:41:57,119
I am listening to you.

461
00:41:57,120 --> 00:41:58,319
Tell me.

462
00:41:58,320 --> 00:42:00,319
We want...

463
00:42:00,320 --> 00:42:03,399
...Kayis to kneel and pledge allegiance like...

464
00:42:03,400 --> 00:42:05,959
...Germiyan, Candar...

465
00:42:05,960 --> 00:42:08,199
...and all other Anatolian Beylics.

466
00:42:09,720 --> 00:42:12,479
Or else..
Or else..

467
00:42:12,920 --> 00:42:14,239
..what?

468
00:42:14,520 --> 00:42:16,239
It will be a shame, Hatun.

469
00:42:18,240 --> 00:42:23,679
For all of you, for all your people,
and for your babies in the cradles.

470
00:42:27,160 --> 00:42:34,559
Either you pledge allegiance, pay the
assigned tax, or you will be destroyed.

471
00:42:34,560 --> 00:42:36,999
Look, envoy.

472
00:42:37,280 --> 00:42:41,639
The Bey of our state, Osman Bey, is at war.

473
00:42:42,000 --> 00:42:45,839
These are matters of state. When he returns...

474
00:42:45,840 --> 00:42:47,319
..you will tell him.

475
00:42:47,880 --> 00:42:49,239
He will come.

476
00:42:49,240 --> 00:42:51,559
He will come and kiss our hands and feet.

477
00:42:51,560 --> 00:42:53,079
Don't worry.

478
00:42:53,080 --> 00:42:55,359
We say the envoy can not be blamed...

479
00:42:55,480 --> 00:42:59,719
...but if you go any further, something
really bad is going to happen to you.

480
00:42:59,880 --> 00:43:02,159
Hatun! -Stop there!

481
00:43:23,080 --> 00:43:24,319
Know your place.

482
00:43:25,000 --> 00:43:29,359
I hope your Bey does not pledge allegiance.

483
00:43:30,320 --> 00:43:34,999
Then I will swim in your blood.

484
00:43:40,440 --> 00:43:41,679
Nokers!

485
00:43:41,680 --> 00:43:44,199
We will go and find Osman! Come on!

486
00:43:59,400 --> 00:44:00,479
Mother...

487
00:44:01,440 --> 00:44:03,119
What will we do now?

488
00:44:03,320 --> 00:44:05,999
They will attack like mad dogs.

489
00:44:07,520 --> 00:44:09,719
We will find a way out my daughter.

490
00:44:10,240 --> 00:44:11,439
Stand tall.

491
00:44:14,640 --> 00:44:17,079
Don't let the enemy sense your fear.

492
00:44:20,920 --> 00:44:21,959
Turhan.

493
00:44:23,120 --> 00:44:25,959
Let's make sure they left. Come on.

494
00:44:27,120 --> 00:44:28,959
As you say, Bala Hatun.

495
00:44:31,840 --> 00:44:34,439
We will keep attacking from all sides.

496
00:44:34,440 --> 00:44:37,839
The infidels won't be able to
take a step beyond the walls.

497
00:44:37,920 --> 00:44:40,839
We will not stop until we make a breach.

498
00:44:42,200 --> 00:44:43,519
Right wing.

499
00:44:44,080 --> 00:44:46,559
Left wing. Are the catapults ready?

500
00:44:46,560 --> 00:44:47,959
The left wing is ready, my Bey.

501
00:44:47,960 --> 00:44:49,599
The right wing is also ready, my Bey.

502
00:44:49,600 --> 00:44:53,039
Our soldiers around the castle have
taken their positions as well, my Bey.

503
00:44:53,040 --> 00:44:54,239
Okay.

504
00:44:54,400 --> 00:44:56,399
Everyone to their duties.

505
00:44:56,640 --> 00:44:59,919
-May our battle be blessed.
-Aameen!

506
00:45:12,840 --> 00:45:19,959
While the catapults hit the walls,
you will watch all around the walls.

507
00:45:20,920 --> 00:45:26,759
If you see a place where a breach
is about to open, you will inform us.

508
00:45:26,760 --> 00:45:28,039
As you order my Bey.

509
00:45:30,040 --> 00:45:31,079
Ayaz

510
00:45:32,640 --> 00:45:34,359
Put the stones.

511
00:45:52,560 --> 00:45:54,279
The time has come.

512
00:45:55,080 --> 00:45:58,919
Today is the most blessed day for us.

513
00:45:59,600 --> 00:46:03,759
Today is the day to take
revenge for the martyrs.

514
00:46:04,000 --> 00:46:10,559
Today is the day to destroy
the enemies spreading poison.

515
00:46:10,560 --> 00:46:11,799
O Allah

516
00:46:13,000 --> 00:46:14,319
Come on, brother!

517
00:46:31,600 --> 00:46:34,039
My Bey has started the attack, brother.

518
00:46:34,560 --> 00:46:36,799
Come on Alps! Come on brothers!

519
00:46:36,800 --> 00:46:39,239
Attack the infidels! Come on!

520
00:46:46,720 --> 00:46:56,399
Allah is the Greatest!

521
00:46:59,880 --> 00:47:03,799
-Saruca Bey. Come on.
-Come on.

522
00:47:04,960 --> 00:47:05,719
Set.

523
00:47:06,440 --> 00:47:07,159
Set.

524
00:47:11,160 --> 00:47:12,919
Come on! Come on

525
00:47:12,920 --> 00:47:15,679
This is for you Lukas!

526
00:47:18,200 --> 00:47:20,399
In the name of Allah!

527
00:47:32,520 --> 00:47:33,639
Osman.

528
00:47:34,000 --> 00:47:38,879
Osman, the dust you raised from
Akhisar will not choke me, but you.

529
00:47:38,880 --> 00:47:41,679
Hristo, take care of the wounded immediately.

530
00:47:41,680 --> 00:47:43,759
Replace the dead ones right away!

531
00:47:43,760 --> 00:47:45,039
Yes, commander.

532
00:47:45,040 --> 00:47:47,559
Soldiers!

533
00:48:03,680 --> 00:48:05,879
Look at our people.

534
00:48:06,480 --> 00:48:09,119
They are really nervous and anxious.

535
00:48:10,520 --> 00:48:13,399
Of course, they are.

536
00:48:13,400 --> 00:48:16,039
They know how cruel the Mongols are.

537
00:48:17,160 --> 00:48:19,959
What can they do? They are scared.

538
00:48:20,640 --> 00:48:21,759
They are cruel.

539
00:48:21,840 --> 00:48:24,719
They attack without caring
if they are young or old.

540
00:48:24,720 --> 00:48:26,639
They attack treacherously.

541
00:48:27,240 --> 00:48:30,799
That's why they come to our
tribe arrogantly asking for taxes.

542
00:48:32,080 --> 00:48:33,759
I don't know the Mongols.

543
00:48:34,920 --> 00:48:40,959
But I know one thing... Osman Bey
will never give them what they want.

544
00:48:43,640 --> 00:48:45,959
We will never bow down, never!

545
00:48:59,280 --> 00:49:03,119
Gather around me. Come on.

546
00:49:10,440 --> 00:49:12,479
First, know this.

547
00:49:13,160 --> 00:49:18,279
Your lives and property are entrusted to us.

548
00:49:20,200 --> 00:49:22,119
May Allah bless you.

549
00:49:23,520 --> 00:49:29,237
When Osman Bey successfully completes the
conquest, he will do what is necessary, God willing.

550
00:49:29,249 --> 00:49:31,159
God willing.

551
00:49:32,080 --> 00:49:37,559
Now the number of Alp
around the tribe will triple.

552
00:49:37,680 --> 00:49:41,039
We will be cautious. We must be.

553
00:49:41,720 --> 00:49:44,319
Everyone, back to your duties.

554
00:49:55,000 --> 00:49:57,439
We will increase the precautions.

555
00:49:57,480 --> 00:49:59,559
The Sisters must stay alert, my Fatma.

556
00:49:59,560 --> 00:50:02,879
Make sure the new ones are well-trained.

557
00:50:03,480 --> 00:50:05,719
Where is Meryem though?

558
00:50:05,760 --> 00:50:08,239
You were going to take her for training...

559
00:50:08,640 --> 00:50:11,519
She was here when the
Mongols came, mother, but...

560
00:50:13,760 --> 00:50:15,479
Maybe she got scared.

561
00:50:16,760 --> 00:50:18,599
We don't know her well but...

562
00:50:19,240 --> 00:50:21,959
You are right. Just in case...

563
00:50:23,160 --> 00:50:27,039
The Sisters will search around
and bring everyone they find, alright?

564
00:50:27,880 --> 00:50:32,199
-Everyone, back to your duties.
-As you order, mother.

565
00:50:37,600 --> 00:50:38,919
O Allah

566
00:50:42,600 --> 00:50:43,719
Hit them

567
00:50:43,920 --> 00:50:47,119
Hit those who took our Baysungur from us!

568
00:50:47,120 --> 00:50:51,919
Hit those who martyred
Bayhan Bey and many others!

569
00:50:52,320 --> 00:50:57,359
Hit, brothers!

570
00:51:04,880 --> 00:51:08,317
The walls of this castle turned out to
be stronger than we thought, my Bey.

571
00:51:08,329 --> 00:51:09,479
Boran!

572
00:51:10,040 --> 00:51:11,359
I am sorry my Bey.

573
00:51:11,560 --> 00:51:14,639
Even if it takes forever we will keep striking.

574
00:51:14,640 --> 00:51:16,239
We will never give up.

575
00:51:17,280 --> 00:51:18,679
Bring my horse.

576
00:51:19,640 --> 00:51:22,519
-I will go and see myself.
-Okay my Bey.

577
00:51:40,200 --> 00:51:41,959
You were right brother.

578
00:51:42,960 --> 00:51:44,959
With these catapults...

579
00:51:45,720 --> 00:51:47,999
...it is impossible to...

580
00:51:48,720 --> 00:51:50,199
...damage these walls.

581
00:51:51,040 --> 00:51:53,919
-Are the masters ready, Hristo?
-They are, commander.

582
00:51:53,920 --> 00:51:55,679
There is a master at every wall.

583
00:51:55,680 --> 00:51:58,536
As soon as there is the
slightest sign of hope for

584
00:51:58,548 --> 00:52:01,359
the Turks, the masters
will repair it immediately.

585
00:52:01,760 --> 00:52:04,719
-Come on. Come on brother!
-Allah is eternal!

586
00:52:05,040 --> 00:52:06,519
Come on lions!

587
00:52:07,640 --> 00:52:09,319
Come on brothers!

588
00:52:09,320 --> 00:52:11,359
We will not lose our hope, come on!

589
00:52:11,360 --> 00:52:15,479
My Allah, may You reward
our efforts. Come on, lions!

590
00:52:15,800 --> 00:52:17,359
Allah is the Greatest!

591
00:52:24,000 --> 00:52:27,719
They could only dust off the
walls with the catapults, sir.

592
00:52:28,040 --> 00:52:31,879
These walls were built by the
greatest craftsmen of Bitynia, Hristo.

593
00:52:31,880 --> 00:52:35,119
They are too strong to be
breached with attacks like this.

594
00:52:35,280 --> 00:52:36,839
Osman will understand that.

595
00:52:36,840 --> 00:52:38,479
He will lose his mind.

596
00:52:38,480 --> 00:52:43,079
I will calm Osman's anger with my
own sword when the Nikea army arrives.

597
00:53:22,600 --> 00:53:24,839
They covered the waterway.

598
00:53:29,600 --> 00:53:32,839
Let's see where the entrance
to this water channel is.

599
00:53:45,040 --> 00:53:47,679
Osman attacked Akhisar.

600
00:53:47,680 --> 00:53:50,039
We are almost there. Commander Toygar.

601
00:53:50,760 --> 00:53:54,359
From now on, Osman will not conquer
any place without our knowledge.

602
00:53:54,360 --> 00:53:57,519
His moves will only be
determined by the Mongols.

603
00:53:57,680 --> 00:54:01,199
He will either pledge
allegiance to us or disappear.

604
00:54:01,200 --> 00:54:03,999
They say Osman never kneels before others.

605
00:54:06,040 --> 00:54:08,759
Who is Osman not to kneel before us?

606
00:54:10,000 --> 00:54:13,679
In our eyes, he is worth less than a mouse.

607
00:54:15,200 --> 00:54:16,959
I want to see Osman.

608
00:54:18,000 --> 00:54:19,039
Come on

609
00:54:25,120 --> 00:54:26,999
Allah is the Greatest!

610
00:54:27,000 --> 00:54:31,759
O Allah

611
00:54:42,910 --> 00:54:47,119
We shoot the target every
time we make a move, for sure!

612
00:54:48,000 --> 00:54:50,799
But brother... -But brother..

613
00:54:51,360 --> 00:54:55,919
The stones we throw do not
even remove the dust of the walls...

614
00:54:56,320 --> 00:54:58,119
...let alone open a breach.

615
00:54:58,120 --> 00:55:00,159
But that breach will be opened eventually.

616
00:55:00,160 --> 00:55:02,279
It will be, but the important thing is to...

617
00:55:02,280 --> 00:55:04,799
...get in that castle before
our men get tired and hopeless.

618
00:55:04,800 --> 00:55:06,799
Right. Right.

619
00:55:08,920 --> 00:55:10,039
Brother..

620
00:55:11,480 --> 00:55:14,559
We need to inform our father. Maybe...

621
00:55:14,760 --> 00:55:16,519
..we can find another way, huh?

622
00:55:16,520 --> 00:55:18,599
It doesn't seem like this will work.

623
00:55:18,800 --> 00:55:20,679
I heard what happened.

624
00:55:30,120 --> 00:55:31,039
Alps!

625
00:55:33,680 --> 00:55:35,039
Gather!

626
00:55:36,000 --> 00:55:37,359
Come here!

627
00:55:40,400 --> 00:55:41,959
Listen well

628
00:55:44,480 --> 00:55:46,359
What's the rule of conquest?

629
00:55:48,160 --> 00:55:51,399
Patience comes from faith in our hearts!

630
00:55:52,000 --> 00:55:55,199
We pray and embrace martyrdom!

631
00:55:56,920 --> 00:55:58,119
For this reason

632
00:55:58,600 --> 00:56:01,559
...I want no despair today!

633
00:56:04,000 --> 00:56:05,519
My sons.

634
00:56:06,440 --> 00:56:07,519
If someone falls

635
00:56:08,160 --> 00:56:09,519
...you get him up.

636
00:56:17,520 --> 00:56:20,679
You never stop until you
make holes in the walls!

637
00:56:21,200 --> 00:56:23,719
You never stop shooting the walls.

638
00:56:24,280 --> 00:56:27,279
Every stone you throw will
make the enemy tremble!

639
00:56:27,880 --> 00:56:29,959
Our determination and tenacity...

640
00:56:30,200 --> 00:56:32,079
...will scare the heathens.

641
00:56:33,000 --> 00:56:34,159
For this reason

642
00:56:35,400 --> 00:56:39,159
...they will be the ones to fall into despair.

643
00:56:43,360 --> 00:56:48,359
When they come out of
those walls like rabid dogs

644
00:56:49,400 --> 00:56:52,919
...they will taste our swords.

645
00:56:55,000 --> 00:56:56,248
Ilbay.

646
00:56:56,260 --> 00:57:00,039
I checked all the walls
my Bey. They are solid.

647
00:57:00,400 --> 00:57:05,639
Yet in the north, there is a water
trough going under the walls.

648
00:57:09,440 --> 00:57:11,119
You say so?

649
00:57:30,200 --> 00:57:32,479
I missed you so much.

650
00:57:34,800 --> 00:57:37,719
Why is Bala still alive? Is there a problem?

651
00:57:40,640 --> 00:57:43,919
I have been waiting for a
message from you for days.

652
00:57:45,520 --> 00:57:47,999
I'm avenging you, mother.

653
00:57:48,960 --> 00:57:54,319
Lullaby, my dear baby.

654
00:57:55,880 --> 00:58:02,239
Sleep well in your dream.

655
00:58:03,520 --> 00:58:06,559
Aunt, I couldn't catch her alone.

656
00:58:07,200 --> 00:58:09,799
-She was always with someone.
-Alright. Alright.

657
00:58:10,480 --> 00:58:12,679
Alright, no problem.

658
00:58:13,320 --> 00:58:14,919
You're among them now.

659
00:58:15,760 --> 00:58:18,879
You can kill whenever you like.

660
00:58:20,160 --> 00:58:21,559
I will kill.

661
00:58:22,280 --> 00:58:26,679
I will kill them and help
my parents rest in peace.

662
00:58:32,440 --> 00:58:34,399
You joined them.

663
00:58:35,400 --> 00:58:37,199
You met them.

664
00:58:38,600 --> 00:58:43,319
-What did you feel?
-Nothing.

665
00:58:44,360 --> 00:58:46,079
I'm angry.

666
00:58:47,120 --> 00:58:48,919
Like you said

667
00:58:49,320 --> 00:58:51,959
...they try to seem good to everyone.

668
00:58:52,720 --> 00:58:57,279
But I know the monster inside them, aunt.

669
00:58:59,680 --> 00:59:01,799
Good, little bird.

670
00:59:02,160 --> 00:59:06,559
Don't let their smiling faces deceive you.

671
00:59:08,520 --> 00:59:10,239
Remember.

672
00:59:14,440 --> 00:59:17,239
I got this prepared by Healer Martin.

673
00:59:20,960 --> 00:59:23,319
For you to sleep well at nights.

674
00:59:24,760 --> 00:59:28,879
Aunt, I couldn't sleep last
night because of nightmares.

675
00:59:29,560 --> 00:59:32,079
What would I do without you?

676
00:59:36,240 --> 00:59:37,639
Poena.

677
00:59:38,200 --> 00:59:39,519
Are you awake?

678
00:59:39,680 --> 00:59:41,599
My name is Halime.

679
00:59:52,800 --> 00:59:55,759
-Poena.
-My name is Halime.

680
01:00:06,240 --> 01:00:08,279
My name is Halime.

681
01:00:21,440 --> 01:00:22,799
Poena.

682
01:00:23,640 --> 01:00:26,919
-What's your name?
-Poena.

683
01:00:37,600 --> 01:00:38,839
Poena...

684
01:00:41,640 --> 01:00:42,959
Come.

685
01:00:44,400 --> 01:00:45,999
Come.

686
01:00:53,920 --> 01:00:56,879
Welcome, little bird.

687
01:01:01,680 --> 01:01:03,199
Again.

688
01:01:04,080 --> 01:01:06,239
-What's your name?
-Poena.

689
01:01:06,480 --> 01:01:08,159
Poena.

690
01:01:09,680 --> 01:01:11,439
Poena..

691
01:01:13,160 --> 01:01:15,719
My hair looks beautiful, right?

692
01:01:16,240 --> 01:01:19,119
Do you want your hair to be like mine?

693
01:01:21,160 --> 01:01:23,199
You heard Poena.

694
01:01:23,720 --> 01:01:26,159
Her hair will be like mine.

695
01:01:30,400 --> 01:01:32,079
My little bird.

696
01:01:32,120 --> 01:01:34,119
Come, come.

697
01:01:50,680 --> 01:01:57,079
Well... What else is happening in their tribe?

698
01:01:58,280 --> 01:02:01,319
Mongolians demand taxes from Osman.

699
01:02:05,440 --> 01:02:07,559
Osman will never accept that.

700
01:02:07,840 --> 01:02:11,679
They didn't respond as
Osman wasn't in the tribe.

701
01:02:12,120 --> 01:02:14,399
They will visit their headquarters.

702
01:02:15,920 --> 01:02:19,359
You've brought me great news, little bird.

703
01:02:23,120 --> 01:02:28,559
Osman, you are in my hands now.

704
01:02:29,600 --> 01:02:31,679
What will you do, aunt?

705
01:02:35,560 --> 01:02:37,359
You'll see.

706
01:02:42,920 --> 01:02:44,439
Now go.

707
01:02:45,920 --> 01:02:48,079
Stay safe.

708
01:02:56,680 --> 01:02:59,199
You're so precious to me.

709
01:03:03,480 --> 01:03:05,599
Come on, come on.

710
01:03:07,320 --> 01:03:11,239
You will never remember your filthy past.

711
01:03:15,480 --> 01:03:18,279
You are my angel of vengeance.

712
01:03:19,040 --> 01:03:22,039
Osman Bey Headquarters

713
01:03:24,600 --> 01:03:29,439
We got a message from Samil patrolling in
the heathen lands beyond Akhisar, my Bey.

714
01:03:31,760 --> 01:03:33,679
The army of Nikea, my Bey

715
01:03:33,840 --> 01:03:36,839
...are marching towards
Akhisar with all their strength.

716
01:03:38,920 --> 01:03:40,319
Lukas...

717
01:03:42,280 --> 01:03:44,519
...gets support from Nikea, huh?

718
01:03:45,640 --> 01:03:47,159
He does, my Bey.

719
01:03:48,440 --> 01:03:51,519
They're going to reach Akhisar soon, my Bey.

720
01:03:54,160 --> 01:03:58,024
While catapults keep shooting
the walls, we can divide

721
01:03:58,036 --> 01:04:01,559
our army and confront
their reinforcements, but...

722
01:04:03,240 --> 01:04:07,479
Of course we will confront them, but...

723
01:04:08,480 --> 01:04:10,759
If we aren't careful

724
01:04:12,000 --> 01:04:17,119
...Lukas may attack as we're outnumbered.

725
01:04:18,560 --> 01:04:24,119
If we don't take action, we'll be an open
target between Lukas and the incoming army.

726
01:04:24,880 --> 01:04:27,839
What's your plan, my Bey?

727
01:04:28,200 --> 01:04:31,359
I will tell, Begum Hatun. I will tell.

728
01:04:33,000 --> 01:04:35,759
We were planning to hit
the walls even for months...

729
01:04:36,080 --> 01:04:40,039
But things have changed. Orhan, Begum Hatun.

730
01:04:40,680 --> 01:04:46,279
You'll take your troops with Yusuf
and Ilbay and confront the army of Nikea.

731
01:04:46,600 --> 01:04:48,399
As you order, my Bey.

732
01:04:48,960 --> 01:04:49,799
But...

733
01:04:51,120 --> 01:04:54,479
In case you fail to stop them,

734
01:04:55,560 --> 01:05:00,239
...we will conquer the fortress by tomorrow.

735
01:05:03,000 --> 01:05:05,799
The water trough Ilbay mentioned...

736
01:05:06,200 --> 01:05:08,079
Boran, Cerkutay. My Bey. My Bey.

737
01:05:08,160 --> 01:05:09,999
You two will get into there...

738
01:05:10,200 --> 01:05:13,119
...and place the Greek fire
under the wall.

739
01:05:15,440 --> 01:05:19,399
The spark we ignite will enlighten the dawn!

740
01:05:19,480 --> 01:05:23,799
The enemy sleeping in
unawareness will be shocked

741
01:05:24,640 --> 01:05:28,039
With Allah's will, Akhisar
will the property of Turks!

742
01:05:28,080 --> 01:05:30,559
-God willing.
-God willing.

743
01:05:35,680 --> 01:05:38,359
Boran Bey, Mongolians are approaching.

744
01:05:38,720 --> 01:05:40,639
Mongolians?

745
01:05:45,560 --> 01:05:49,439
Brother... What are they doing here, Cerkutay?

746
01:05:54,920 --> 01:05:57,879
Alps, stand on alert.

747
01:06:06,560 --> 01:06:08,199
Toygar.

748
01:06:09,360 --> 01:06:10,639
Toygar?

749
01:06:11,200 --> 01:06:12,959
Do you know that dog?

750
01:06:15,320 --> 01:06:17,639
The butcher of Mongolians.

751
01:06:24,400 --> 01:06:26,199
Brother.

752
01:06:28,560 --> 01:06:31,679
It's not good that he's come here.

753
01:06:48,080 --> 01:06:51,319
What are you doing here? Why did you come?

754
01:06:52,640 --> 01:06:56,479
Cerkutay, born as a Mongolian with bad blood.

755
01:06:57,520 --> 01:07:02,359
Don't be afraid. I'm not here for you.
I will teach Osman who his master is!

756
01:07:05,120 --> 01:07:06,679
So...

757
01:07:07,680 --> 01:07:09,079
Where is he?

758
01:07:09,880 --> 01:07:12,799
Dogs like you never walk without their masters.

759
01:07:13,160 --> 01:07:16,359
Cerkutay, you are a fiery boy.

760
01:07:16,800 --> 01:07:22,079
You used to burn too fast like now. That's
why I like your brother more than you.

761
01:07:25,560 --> 01:07:27,279
His brother?

762
01:07:31,320 --> 01:07:32,559
Cerkutay.

763
01:07:42,800 --> 01:07:46,479
Don't mention my brother's name...

764
01:07:47,880 --> 01:07:51,719
...with your filthy mouth. Don't.

765
01:07:53,160 --> 01:07:57,439
He said you made this
yourself and gave it to him.

766
01:08:02,240 --> 01:08:07,159
He's deeply ashamed that
he's the brother of traitor like you.

767
01:08:18,160 --> 01:08:21,078
He's dying to take revenge.

768
01:08:22,640 --> 01:08:24,839
-Shut up!
-Cerkutay.

769
01:08:25,640 --> 01:08:28,999
-Brother. Brother.
-Cerkutay.

770
01:08:29,200 --> 01:08:34,118
You are a dog whose leash
Osman is holding, Cerkutay.

771
01:08:34,960 --> 01:08:37,959
I know you can't take this
dagger out of the sheath.

772
01:08:38,439 --> 01:08:42,439
Cerkutay, brother! Brother!

773
01:08:43,240 --> 01:08:49,278
Look... If you want to leave here
with your head on your shoulders,

774
01:08:51,120 --> 01:08:52,919
...don't say another word.

775
01:08:53,160 --> 01:08:55,198
Just tell me what you want.

776
01:08:55,560 --> 01:08:59,118
You don't have a tiny piece of courage.

777
01:09:00,439 --> 01:09:03,639
Inform Osman. I'm the messenger of Mongolians.

778
01:09:03,960 --> 01:09:05,919
I will talk to him.

779
01:09:08,359 --> 01:09:09,999
Wait here.

780
01:09:26,279 --> 01:09:29,359
-Do I have permission, my Bey?
-Come in, Boran.

781
01:09:34,880 --> 01:09:38,118
My Bey, a Mongolian called Toygar...

782
01:09:44,760 --> 01:09:47,319
Easy! Easy

783
01:09:56,120 --> 01:09:57,639
Just wait.

784
01:10:07,080 --> 01:10:09,039
Osman.

785
01:10:12,160 --> 01:10:16,279
I see that you've forgotten
the power of Mongolians...

786
01:10:17,000 --> 01:10:19,479
...and keep having raids.

787
01:10:30,880 --> 01:10:33,519
I neither forget the past...

788
01:10:34,480 --> 01:10:37,559
...nor stay away from
what awaits me in the future.

789
01:10:42,920 --> 01:10:45,159
Your name is Toygar, huh?

790
01:10:46,160 --> 01:10:47,839
Tell me now.

791
01:10:48,240 --> 01:10:52,919
The one who sent you here as the
messenger... What does he demand?

792
01:11:15,240 --> 01:11:19,799
Olcaytu Khan's mightiest commander...

793
01:11:20,680 --> 01:11:23,079
...Ulugan has sent me.

794
01:11:33,200 --> 01:11:35,399
You should know, Osman

795
01:11:37,520 --> 01:11:40,439
...Ulugan never demands.

796
01:11:41,720 --> 01:11:43,519
But he takes.

797
01:11:48,880 --> 01:11:51,639
From you, we will take..

798
01:11:57,800 --> 01:12:01,999
...loyalty oath to Mongolians and...

799
01:12:02,720 --> 01:12:08,399
...ten carts of gold per year as the tax.

800
01:12:14,320 --> 01:12:17,359
It's you who forgot the past.

801
01:12:20,440 --> 01:12:22,279
Your commander..

802
01:12:23,200 --> 01:12:25,559
Doesn't he know...

803
01:12:26,320 --> 01:12:33,359
...Kayi never paid Mongolians a single coin...

804
01:12:34,960 --> 01:12:37,679
...or pledged loyalty!

805
01:12:38,240 --> 01:12:41,999
Ulugan isn't like other Mongolians, Osman.

806
01:12:45,360 --> 01:12:47,719
He'll both take the gold...

807
01:12:51,280 --> 01:12:53,959
...and make you kneel.

808
01:12:57,080 --> 01:12:58,119
Ask...

809
01:13:02,520 --> 01:13:04,439
...your dog Cerkutay.

810
01:13:05,440 --> 01:13:07,239
He will tell you.

811
01:13:08,040 --> 01:13:09,679
Look at me!

812
01:13:11,680 --> 01:13:14,119
You're here as the messenger.

813
01:13:14,800 --> 01:13:16,999
Don't push my patience.

814
01:13:18,920 --> 01:13:21,279
Now go tell your commander...

815
01:13:22,480 --> 01:13:28,079
...Osman doesn't accept any of your demands!

816
01:13:31,360 --> 01:13:33,639
We didn't demand, Osman

817
01:13:35,000 --> 01:13:39,119
...but just told you what we'll do next.

818
01:13:47,160 --> 01:13:48,639
My Bey.

819
01:13:49,000 --> 01:13:52,159
Those jackals set their eyes on us.

820
01:13:53,480 --> 01:13:56,559
They'll attempt to jump on us soon.

821
01:13:57,440 --> 01:13:59,479
You're right.

822
01:14:01,400 --> 01:14:03,039
-Alaaddin.
-My Bey.

823
01:14:03,120 --> 01:14:04,919
Go to the tribe quickly.

824
01:14:06,440 --> 01:14:08,839
You never know what they can do.

825
01:14:09,600 --> 01:14:11,559
Tell everyone to be more careful.

826
01:14:12,080 --> 01:14:14,199
As you order, my Bey.

827
01:14:27,840 --> 01:14:32,079
God willing, we'll get great news
about the conquest of Akhisar soon.

828
01:14:32,080 --> 01:14:33,519
-God willing.
-God willing.

829
01:14:33,680 --> 01:14:37,279
Until that time, we'll keep
tighter security around the tribe.

830
01:14:37,840 --> 01:14:42,279
We placed watchmen inside and outside
the soup kitchen and the healing tent.

831
01:14:42,280 --> 01:14:44,679
-Just in case.
-Good, girl.

832
01:14:44,840 --> 01:14:48,159
Be careful. I want no mistakes.

833
01:14:48,920 --> 01:14:52,319
You never know what vile
things Mongolians can do.

834
01:14:52,640 --> 01:14:56,839
Yes, Cerkutay always tells me
about the cruelty of those nokers.

835
01:14:57,320 --> 01:15:00,279
He still can't believe how he stayed among them.

836
01:15:03,240 --> 01:15:05,999
-Is Cerkutay Bey a Mongolian?
-Yes.

837
01:15:07,880 --> 01:15:09,719
I'm surprised.

838
01:15:10,280 --> 01:15:14,639
-He was with those cruel Mongolians...
-You never know who can do what, Holofira.

839
01:15:14,760 --> 01:15:17,279
You came from the castle of the lord.

840
01:15:20,080 --> 01:15:22,399
Still no news from Meryem?

841
01:15:23,480 --> 01:15:25,279
Do I have permission Bala Hatun?

842
01:15:25,640 --> 01:15:27,279
Come in

843
01:15:31,760 --> 01:15:32,919
Bala Hatun.

844
01:15:33,000 --> 01:15:36,719
-Alps found Meryem. She was in Sogut.
-Let her in.

845
01:15:37,720 --> 01:15:39,639
As you order, Bala Hatun.

846
01:15:52,320 --> 01:15:54,479
What were you doing in Sogut, Meryem?

847
01:15:55,440 --> 01:15:58,439
Why did you leave the
tribe without my knowledge?

848
01:15:58,760 --> 01:16:00,559
Forgive me, Bala Hatun.

849
01:16:00,600 --> 01:16:04,279
I felt scared as Mongolians came here.

850
01:16:22,960 --> 01:16:25,439
Don't cry, girl.

851
01:16:28,760 --> 01:16:30,319
Take this.

852
01:16:35,840 --> 01:16:39,639
Now tell me everything.
Obviously, you were scared.

853
01:16:41,720 --> 01:16:46,359
I wanted to see my grandmother.
I have nobody else, anyway.

854
01:16:48,600 --> 01:16:52,399
I visited her grave and hugged.

855
01:16:56,640 --> 01:16:58,559
I miss her so much.

856
01:16:59,120 --> 01:17:02,799
I promise I won't go anywhere
without informing again.

857
01:17:07,480 --> 01:17:12,279
This time, I ignore it because of
your age and inexperience, Meryem.

858
01:17:14,720 --> 01:17:15,759
But...

859
01:17:16,800 --> 01:17:21,279
...when you're scared come to us, right?

860
01:17:22,360 --> 01:17:26,759
When you want to visit your
grandmother, you go to her with the Alps.

861
01:17:27,240 --> 01:17:29,999
Thank you, Bala Hatun. May Allah bless you.

862
01:17:35,080 --> 01:17:38,279
May Allah not let any of
His servants be all alone.

863
01:17:47,520 --> 01:17:48,759
Meryem.

864
01:17:49,440 --> 01:17:51,679
You are not alone.

865
01:17:55,040 --> 01:17:58,479
Mother, if you allow me...

866
01:18:00,080 --> 01:18:02,439
I want Meryem to be my helper.

867
01:18:02,680 --> 01:18:03,959
Really?

868
01:18:05,960 --> 01:18:07,599
I would really want that.

869
01:18:16,760 --> 01:18:19,959
Of course I allow you, my daughter.

870
01:18:20,760 --> 01:18:22,279
From now on...

871
01:18:23,520 --> 01:18:25,719
Meryem will be your helper.

872
01:18:26,440 --> 01:18:29,399
She will always be by your side.

873
01:18:32,720 --> 01:18:36,199
I will fulfill my duty properly, Bala Hatun.

874
01:18:57,720 --> 01:18:59,399
Who are you?

875
01:19:00,360 --> 01:19:03,239
What are you doing here
in the middle of the night?

876
01:19:20,600 --> 01:19:25,279
Alps! Be the nightmare of those who are
dreaming of making Osman Bey bow down

877
01:19:25,280 --> 01:19:26,599
Attack!

878
01:19:26,600 --> 01:19:29,999
Nokers, attack!

879
01:19:40,280 --> 01:19:44,999
May demons take your life, Osman!
I will punish you with my wrath!

880
01:19:50,120 --> 01:19:52,919
You will not get away with this, Osman!

881
01:19:53,120 --> 01:19:55,759
You will see the power of the Mongols!

882
01:20:12,640 --> 01:20:16,759
Toygar will make Osman pay for this.

883
01:20:28,600 --> 01:20:32,199
I spilled your dirty blood for this.

884
01:20:41,280 --> 01:20:48,519
The Mongol blood on my sword will
become Osman's curse and will haunt him.

885
01:20:48,520 --> 01:20:49,839
Come on

886
01:20:56,800 --> 01:20:59,679
My Bey, Begum Hatun and Ilbay came.

887
01:21:01,960 --> 01:21:03,079
My Bey.

888
01:21:10,920 --> 01:21:12,079
Ayaz.

889
01:21:16,760 --> 01:21:18,439
Where is my father Ayaz?

890
01:21:18,440 --> 01:21:22,159
There was no one entering or
leaving since the guard shift, my Bey.

891
01:21:24,000 --> 01:21:26,039
Nothing bad happened, God willing.

892
01:21:31,120 --> 01:21:32,279
Aykurt.

893
01:21:33,720 --> 01:21:34,959
My Shahzade(Prince)

894
01:21:35,720 --> 01:21:37,639
Where is my Osman Bey, Aykurt?

895
01:21:38,720 --> 01:21:40,399
I don't know my Shahzade(Prince).

896
01:21:44,320 --> 01:21:46,399
Where would he go alone during a war?

897
01:22:05,480 --> 01:22:08,229
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate.

898
01:22:08,229 --> 01:22:10,679
May Allah bless you, my son.

899
01:22:10,680 --> 01:22:13,439
I bothered you..
Why would this bother me, mother?

900
01:22:13,440 --> 01:22:14,799
Don't say that.

901
01:22:27,400 --> 01:22:28,599
My son.

902
01:22:33,320 --> 01:22:34,559
Here, my son.

903
01:22:34,800 --> 01:22:39,439
Do not bother, mother. Mother. Sit down.

904
01:22:42,880 --> 01:22:47,039
-Son, is the soup good?
-It's good.

905
01:22:52,960 --> 01:22:54,999
Thank you, son.

906
01:22:55,120 --> 01:22:56,839
May no stones touch your feet.

907
01:22:56,840 --> 01:22:59,079
May your hands never see hardship, mother.

908
01:22:59,080 --> 01:23:00,479
May they never see hardship.

909
01:23:00,480 --> 01:23:03,519
Tell me. Who are you?

910
01:23:07,320 --> 01:23:13,799
I am a servant of Allah, striving
for the state on Allah's path.

911
01:23:13,800 --> 01:23:16,479
Tell me mother.
Don't you have...

912
01:23:16,480 --> 01:23:19,559
...a husband or a son to
take care of these for you?

913
01:23:19,560 --> 01:23:24,959
My husband was martyred in
deceased Ertugrul Bey's army...

914
01:23:25,320 --> 01:23:30,359
...and my son was martyred
in the path of our Osman Bey...

915
01:23:30,360 --> 01:23:32,199
...the ruler of our state.

916
01:23:39,200 --> 01:23:42,159
Only this orphan was left behind.

917
01:23:43,360 --> 01:23:44,999
Once his hands hold a sword...

918
01:23:45,000 --> 01:23:48,199
...I will also sacrifice him for the state.

919
01:23:51,880 --> 01:23:53,319
Mother.

920
01:23:57,680 --> 01:23:58,759
Mother.

921
01:24:06,280 --> 01:24:08,719
As long as mothers like you exist...

922
01:24:11,520 --> 01:24:13,679
...this state..

923
01:24:14,800 --> 01:24:16,599
..even if all of them come..

924
01:24:17,440 --> 01:24:19,559
...even if all the enemies come...

925
01:24:19,680 --> 01:24:23,399
...no one can make us kneel.
-Thank you.

926
01:24:24,200 --> 01:24:27,759
May you and our children always be there.

927
01:24:29,440 --> 01:24:31,079
Do you need food, son?

928
01:24:32,600 --> 01:24:35,719
-Come and eat.
-I do, mother.

929
01:24:36,520 --> 01:24:37,679
I am in need.

930
01:24:41,760 --> 01:24:43,719
They call me Osman Bey.

931
01:24:47,320 --> 01:24:49,359
Many soldiers stand behind me.

932
01:24:49,640 --> 01:24:51,799
I am in need of your prayers.

933
01:24:53,280 --> 01:24:54,919
My Osman Bey.

934
01:24:55,760 --> 01:25:00,519
Open your hands. Mother.

935
01:25:01,520 --> 01:25:02,719
Pray for me...

936
01:25:03,320 --> 01:25:05,479
..and all my valiants..

937
01:25:05,880 --> 01:25:07,399
...behind me.

938
01:25:08,560 --> 01:25:10,319
Our wars..

939
01:25:10,600 --> 01:25:14,359
...will reach victory through
the prayers of mothers like you.

940
01:25:19,920 --> 01:25:21,439
Pray..

941
01:25:28,120 --> 01:25:29,239
My son.

942
01:25:29,480 --> 01:25:30,959
Come here.

943
01:26:18,000 --> 01:26:19,159
Brother..

944
01:26:19,600 --> 01:26:20,759
...what happened?

945
01:26:22,320 --> 01:26:26,639
What are you thinking about while
we are here on duty, Cerkutay?

946
01:26:30,320 --> 01:26:31,879
I buried...

947
01:26:33,160 --> 01:26:34,799
...Mongol Cerkutay...

948
01:26:35,280 --> 01:26:37,879
..and my past. But...

949
01:26:38,400 --> 01:26:39,559
But..

950
01:26:39,960 --> 01:26:42,639
...your past does not
let you go, right, brother?

951
01:26:45,880 --> 01:26:48,479
We thought you had no one.

952
01:26:48,920 --> 01:26:51,879
Why did you hide that you
had a brother for so long?

953
01:26:56,120 --> 01:26:58,799
I'll tell you one day.

954
01:27:01,400 --> 01:27:02,919
But what will change?

955
01:27:02,920 --> 01:27:05,319
He sees me as his enemy.

956
01:27:11,080 --> 01:27:13,519
Brother. Don't be upset.

957
01:27:14,200 --> 01:27:16,879
He'll understand you in time.

958
01:27:18,720 --> 01:27:20,079
We'll see.

959
01:27:20,880 --> 01:27:23,399
But that's not the only problem, brother.

960
01:27:23,520 --> 01:27:25,719
Hard days are waiting for us, Boran.

961
01:27:27,720 --> 01:27:29,039
Those Mongols..

962
01:27:29,680 --> 01:27:30,839
That man...

963
01:27:32,840 --> 01:27:35,399
...never leave before he takes what he wants.

964
01:27:35,640 --> 01:27:36,919
Brother..

965
01:27:37,400 --> 01:27:40,599
When did the wolves let jackals hunt, brother?

966
01:27:40,600 --> 01:27:44,399
We'll be the death of those who
disturb our peace, my Cerkutay.

967
01:27:45,040 --> 01:27:46,079
For sure.

968
01:27:49,200 --> 01:27:52,239
Then now...

969
01:27:52,920 --> 01:27:54,999
...we will destroy these walls.

970
01:27:56,560 --> 01:28:01,559
We'll bring honor to Akhisar,
the place ruled by dark spirits...

971
01:28:01,560 --> 01:28:03,599
...with Islam.

972
01:28:03,600 --> 01:28:05,879
God willing, brother, God willing.

973
01:28:08,120 --> 01:28:09,359
Brother..

974
01:28:09,440 --> 01:28:12,039
...the sun has begun to show itself, Cerkutay.

975
01:28:13,240 --> 01:28:14,279
Come on.

976
01:28:14,600 --> 01:28:18,439
Let's place the Greek fire around thoroughly.

977
01:28:18,440 --> 01:28:20,199
Come on.

978
01:28:59,400 --> 01:29:00,999
Brother.

979
01:29:06,320 --> 01:29:08,719
Put it in brother.

980
01:29:16,800 --> 01:29:18,679
Come on brother.

981
01:29:18,680 --> 01:29:21,639
That one. That one.

982
01:29:27,960 --> 01:29:31,059
-Praise be!
-Alright.

983
01:29:53,680 --> 01:29:56,639
You are done Osman!

984
01:29:57,160 --> 01:30:00,759
You sealed your own death warrant!

985
01:30:01,080 --> 01:30:05,119
You declared war not only on
me but on the Mongol state as well

986
01:30:24,840 --> 01:30:28,079
Take this. Take this to Commander Ulugan.

987
01:30:28,440 --> 01:30:32,559
When he receives the letter, he
will come here with all his armies.

988
01:30:37,440 --> 01:30:38,679
Nokers!

989
01:30:38,680 --> 01:30:40,439
Draw your swords!

990
01:30:43,920 --> 01:30:46,639
For blood, for death..

991
01:30:46,720 --> 01:30:48,599
...swing your swords!

992
01:30:48,600 --> 01:30:51,719
Blood! Blood! Blood!

993
01:30:51,720 --> 01:30:55,439
Tonight, we will shed blood

994
01:30:55,440 --> 01:31:02,879
And so much blood will be shed that we will
witness the sunrise in a pool of blood.

995
01:31:03,400 --> 01:31:07,079
We will burn and destroy
all the tribes that we find.

996
01:31:07,120 --> 01:31:10,719
Osman will pay for what he did

997
01:31:11,560 --> 01:31:12,919
Set out!

998
01:31:19,120 --> 01:31:21,119
-Osman Bey Headquarters-

999
01:31:22,920 --> 01:31:24,679
He is not around, my Shahzade(Prince).

1000
01:31:24,680 --> 01:31:29,159
We looked everywhere. There are
no tracks. And Iltutan is not in his place.

1001
01:31:32,320 --> 01:31:33,599
Orhan Bey.

1002
01:31:33,600 --> 01:31:35,639
What if something bad happened?

1003
01:31:36,360 --> 01:31:38,929
Do we need to send Alps,
my Shahzade(Prince)?

1004
01:31:41,080 --> 01:31:45,319
Attention! Osman Bey!

1005
01:31:46,920 --> 01:31:47,999
My Bey...

1006
01:31:49,880 --> 01:31:52,399
We were so worried when we could not find you.

1007
01:31:52,400 --> 01:31:55,079
We thought an important thing happened.

1008
01:31:55,280 --> 01:31:58,199
Conquests are not just for castles.

1009
01:31:58,200 --> 01:32:01,279
First of all, it is for the hearts.

1010
01:32:02,040 --> 01:32:06,159
Well, we shed a lot of blood and sweat for this.

1011
01:32:06,160 --> 01:32:10,359
But behind us are our people with prayers
in their hearts and tears in their eyes.

1012
01:32:10,360 --> 01:32:12,279
We should not forget them.

1013
01:32:12,560 --> 01:32:13,959
Okay, my Bey.

1014
01:32:15,440 --> 01:32:16,679
Send news to Bala.

1015
01:32:16,680 --> 01:32:19,279
She should establish a foundation immediately.

1016
01:32:19,280 --> 01:32:21,479
She should take care of everything personally.

1017
01:32:21,480 --> 01:32:23,959
We will solve all the problems of our people...

1018
01:32:24,720 --> 01:32:27,079
...with that foundation God willing.

1019
01:32:27,320 --> 01:32:28,679
As you order my Bey.

1020
01:32:31,320 --> 01:32:35,359
It is time to make our final move for Akhisar...

1021
01:32:36,840 --> 01:32:39,479
...which we've been surrounding for a long time.

1022
01:32:52,760 --> 01:32:56,439
Raid!

1023
01:33:21,640 --> 01:33:27,679
Kill them all! Show them
the furor of Erlik Khan!

1024
01:33:31,200 --> 01:33:34,039
Mother... Wake up

1025
01:33:56,840 --> 01:33:59,479
Wake up mother! Wake up

1026
01:34:36,400 --> 01:34:38,959
The dog whose time has come looks for its owner.

1027
01:34:39,080 --> 01:34:41,239
And you called for your owner, Osman.

1028
01:34:41,320 --> 01:34:43,799
You will be disciplined with blood.

1029
01:34:53,740 --> 01:34:56,148
Did you feel anything
wrong or strange while...

1030
01:34:56,148 --> 01:34:58,949
...placing the Greek fire
at the base of the walls?

1031
01:34:58,950 --> 01:35:00,359
No my Bey.

1032
01:35:00,360 --> 01:35:02,479
Those dogs didn't even notice.

1033
01:35:02,480 --> 01:35:06,239
They trust the walls they
hide behind so much, my Bey.

1034
01:35:09,240 --> 01:35:11,919
They seem to be in a deep sleep of unawareness.

1035
01:35:12,320 --> 01:35:17,199
It won't just be the cold frost that wakes
them from their sleep of unawareness.

1036
01:35:17,480 --> 01:35:21,039
When the breach is open... Saruca.
-My Bey...

1037
01:35:21,320 --> 01:35:24,679
You will get in with the army.
-Yes my Bey.

1038
01:35:28,960 --> 01:35:30,479
Come on lions.

1039
01:35:31,160 --> 01:35:32,359
Get ready.

1040
01:35:32,840 --> 01:35:36,119
Come on!

1041
01:35:44,520 --> 01:35:46,599
What is the latest situation, Hristo?

1042
01:35:46,600 --> 01:35:49,639
The catapult fire continued
until morning, Commander.

1043
01:35:49,640 --> 01:35:54,679
But only briefly during the night, and just
now, the attacks from the right wing stopped.

1044
01:35:55,720 --> 01:35:58,479
During the night and just now, right?

1045
01:36:00,840 --> 01:36:04,039
Commander, the Turks are
approaching from the right wing.

1046
01:36:24,160 --> 01:36:26,039
Did the walls take any damage?

1047
01:36:26,560 --> 01:36:29,719
-Why did they come here?
-The walls are strong, sir.

1048
01:36:29,800 --> 01:36:31,359
We just checked.

1049
01:36:34,560 --> 01:36:40,719
So, Osman is coming to his death, huh, Hristo?

1050
01:36:44,280 --> 01:36:45,439
Lukas!

1051
01:36:47,640 --> 01:36:50,679
Let's see if these walls
can protect you from me.

1052
01:36:50,680 --> 01:36:53,839
They are within our range. Archers!

1053
01:37:02,790 --> 01:37:04,279
The channel..

1054
01:37:04,280 --> 01:37:05,439
It's a trap!

1055
01:37:05,440 --> 01:37:08,039
Get off the walls immediately! It's a trap!

1056
01:37:42,000 --> 01:37:45,559
The real owners of the Holy Roman Empire

1057
01:37:46,040 --> 01:37:54,519
To protect what is yours, to stop the Turks,
you will fight to the last drop of your blood!

1058
01:37:57,040 --> 01:37:58,319
Come, Osman, come!

1059
01:37:58,320 --> 01:38:00,359
Come to your death

1060
01:38:00,360 --> 01:38:05,159
O Allah! Come on valiants!

1061
01:38:05,160 --> 01:38:08,799
Attack!

1062
01:39:33,320 --> 01:39:35,439
Damn it.

1063
01:39:35,440 --> 01:39:36,799
Where are you Sofia?

1064
01:39:45,360 --> 01:39:50,399
We will attack from behind with the
Nikea troops and divide Osman's units.

1065
01:39:51,800 --> 01:39:54,679
Lukas will attack with his armies...

1066
01:39:55,400 --> 01:39:57,999
...and make Osman suffer in hell.

1067
01:39:59,480 --> 01:40:02,679
Osman will die between
these two armies today, Sofia.

1068
01:40:03,160 --> 01:40:04,479
There's no way out.

1069
01:40:14,080 --> 01:40:16,759
They are approaching with the Nikea troops.

1070
01:40:16,760 --> 01:40:18,959
And that witch Sofia is leading them.

1071
01:40:19,440 --> 01:40:20,479
Good.

1072
01:40:20,640 --> 01:40:23,439
It's time for that head to be cut off.

1073
01:40:23,680 --> 01:40:25,599
Yes, Begum Hatun.

1074
01:40:26,360 --> 01:40:30,999
The jackal fighting with the wolf
throws up blood when the time comes.

1075
01:40:35,520 --> 01:40:36,759
Ilbay...

1076
01:40:37,320 --> 01:40:38,959
...now it's your turn.

1077
01:40:39,320 --> 01:40:42,199
Alps, we will stop them. Let's go.

1078
01:40:49,320 --> 01:40:51,119
Come now.

1079
01:40:51,360 --> 01:40:53,599
Your death is waiting for you here.

1080
01:41:08,640 --> 01:41:09,879
Now!

1081
01:41:12,440 --> 01:41:13,879
What is happening?

1082
01:41:21,840 --> 01:41:26,039
Where are they?

1083
01:41:27,760 --> 01:41:31,439
Bring the shields.

1084
01:41:34,600 --> 01:41:37,959
Come on, Begum Hatun. It's time.

1085
01:41:37,960 --> 01:41:43,959
Let's go, Alps! Allah is the Greatest!

1086
01:42:19,560 --> 01:42:22,359
Come on Alps! Come on valiants!

1087
01:42:22,720 --> 01:42:26,719
Before your sword sheds blood,
your head will be cut off, you witch.

1088
01:42:26,720 --> 01:42:30,679
Begum, so I start the slaughter with you, huh?

1089
01:43:03,680 --> 01:43:06,439
Someone's coming. Who are they?

1090
01:43:15,240 --> 01:43:19,399
It's Samil. Samil is coming.

1091
01:43:19,840 --> 01:43:21,639
Come on Ilbay! Come on

1092
01:43:22,680 --> 01:43:24,439
Show no mercy to the infidels.

1093
01:43:24,440 --> 01:43:28,399
Today, the fire of the infidels will be
extinguished. Allah is the Greatest!

1094
01:43:49,320 --> 01:43:51,519
-Praise be!
-My Shahzade(Prince).

1095
01:43:51,560 --> 01:43:55,239
-Thanks, Samil.
-I'd sacrifice my life for our Bey and Kayis.

1096
01:43:55,360 --> 01:43:58,079
Thank you, thank you.
Swing your sword then.

1097
01:43:58,200 --> 01:44:00,239
-Come on.
-Alright.

1098
01:44:01,000 --> 01:44:02,359
Alps!

1099
01:44:02,480 --> 01:44:04,919
The gate of conquest is here!

1100
01:44:04,960 --> 01:44:06,759
Attack the nest of heathens!

1101
01:44:06,800 --> 01:44:08,919
Allah is the greatest!

1102
01:44:09,000 --> 01:44:13,559
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!

1103
01:44:22,920 --> 01:44:26,119
-Open the gate! Come on!
-Alaaddin.

1104
01:44:26,840 --> 01:44:30,119
-Something's wrong, mother.
-We'll see.

1105
01:44:30,840 --> 01:44:34,159
Alaaddin. Alaaddin.

1106
01:44:36,360 --> 01:44:40,079
-Osman, Orhan.. Are they alright?
-Everybody is fine, thanks to Allah.

1107
01:44:40,840 --> 01:44:43,679
We besieged the fortress, but...

1108
01:44:44,880 --> 01:44:48,359
...Mongolians are back in the frontiers.

1109
01:44:48,920 --> 01:44:52,319
Their impertinent messenger
appeared before my father.

1110
01:44:52,560 --> 01:44:56,079
He came to the tribe
earlier. I just sent him away.

1111
01:44:56,280 --> 01:44:59,239
And we're keeping tighter
security. The tribe is safe.

1112
01:44:59,600 --> 01:45:01,839
Well done, mother.

1113
01:45:02,480 --> 01:45:05,599
You never know what
those rabid cannibals can do.

1114
01:45:06,200 --> 01:45:09,119
-We should be careful.
-Yes.

1115
01:45:13,840 --> 01:45:15,679
Bala Hatun

1116
01:45:16,120 --> 01:45:19,479
-My Shahzade(Prince).
-Turahan?

1117
01:45:21,680 --> 01:45:25,399
-Turahan, what's the matter?
-My Shahzade(Prince), bad news.

1118
01:45:26,240 --> 01:45:29,079
Mongolians raided the villages of Turks.

1119
01:45:30,400 --> 01:45:33,039
-What?
-They burned them down.

1120
01:45:34,920 --> 01:45:37,199
Vile dogs

1121
01:45:46,240 --> 01:45:51,399
You will wish you had never
destroyed this wall, Osman.

1122
01:45:53,000 --> 01:45:55,479
You will wish you had never met me.

1123
01:46:00,520 --> 01:46:02,839
Waiting for support from Nikea?

1124
01:46:03,240 --> 01:46:05,119
It's over!

1125
01:46:10,000 --> 01:46:11,759
You're on your own.

1126
01:46:20,160 --> 01:46:23,359
I'll send you to hell where you came from.

1127
01:46:23,520 --> 01:46:26,359
You can't bite me off.

1128
01:46:52,160 --> 01:46:53,839
You're going to die, Turk.

1129
01:46:54,200 --> 01:46:58,719
There is no tribe but death and
no ending but eternity, commander.

1130
01:46:58,800 --> 01:47:04,679
Now we will see who dies and who survives.

1131
01:47:04,720 --> 01:47:07,239
You'll never find peace in this land.

1132
01:47:07,680 --> 01:47:10,359
Come here, come.

1133
01:47:28,120 --> 01:47:31,039
Come to me. Come.

1134
01:47:44,880 --> 01:47:48,119
We'll never find peace in this land, huh?

1135
01:47:48,880 --> 01:47:52,799
It doesn't matter even if the
cruel loom over us like a storm!

1136
01:47:53,280 --> 01:47:58,279
We'll beat despair with our faith
and be victorious, for sure!

1137
01:47:58,560 --> 01:48:03,439
We'll break your evil and
make hope prevail in this land.

1138
01:48:04,040 --> 01:48:08,079
But you will never see that.

1139
01:48:15,520 --> 01:48:17,399
Dog.

1140
01:48:23,080 --> 01:48:26,959
-Attack, warriors!
-Stick your swords into dark chests of heathens!

1141
01:48:27,120 --> 01:48:29,279
Don't let them pass!

1142
01:48:29,760 --> 01:48:33,559
The jackal rising against
the wolf will be devastated!

1143
01:48:33,640 --> 01:48:37,559
And the world will flourish with
the glorious weapons of Kayis!

1144
01:48:51,040 --> 01:48:53,359
Damn it!

1145
01:49:01,080 --> 01:49:04,759
You won't be able to enjoy your
victory due to Mongolians, Osman.

1146
01:49:06,880 --> 01:49:08,679
Sofia is running off!

1147
01:49:12,560 --> 01:49:15,159
We will kill her one day.

1148
01:49:17,040 --> 01:49:18,519
Let's go.

1149
01:49:22,400 --> 01:49:25,759
Alps, keep your eyes wide open around the tribe!

1150
01:49:26,480 --> 01:49:29,399
Turahan, hold all the ways coming to the tribe.

1151
01:49:29,720 --> 01:49:33,479
Alps should carry the Greek fire just in case.

1152
01:49:33,480 --> 01:49:35,079
As you order, my Shahzade(Prince).

1153
01:49:35,560 --> 01:49:36,759
Come on, alps.

1154
01:49:37,400 --> 01:49:39,399
-Mother.
-Son.

1155
01:49:42,320 --> 01:49:44,199
Take care of the tribe, mother.

1156
01:49:44,360 --> 01:49:46,759
I will go fast and inform my father.

1157
01:49:47,160 --> 01:49:50,719
Be careful, Alaaddin. Don't worry, mother.

1158
01:49:51,680 --> 01:49:54,319
-Gonca.
-Alaaddin.

1159
01:50:00,040 --> 01:50:03,079
-Have a safe journey, my Bey.
-Thanks, hatun.

1160
01:50:03,360 --> 01:50:05,519
May Allah protect you.

1161
01:50:05,760 --> 01:50:07,079
Here we go.

1162
01:50:07,240 --> 01:50:09,039
Let's go!

1163
01:50:15,880 --> 01:50:17,519
Stay safe

1164
01:50:17,720 --> 01:50:20,439
Come on, come on

1165
01:50:32,760 --> 01:50:34,439
My Allah..

1166
01:50:37,120 --> 01:50:40,799
You couldn't get used to it yet?

1167
01:50:41,720 --> 01:50:45,999
Your heart hurts whenever
Alaaddin goes on a mission.

1168
01:50:48,240 --> 01:50:50,279
I couldn't, mother.

1169
01:50:53,680 --> 01:50:55,999
How did you get used to it?

1170
01:51:00,520 --> 01:51:03,359
Your husband and sons are always fighting.

1171
01:51:03,600 --> 01:51:07,359
Tell me. How do you endure this, mother?

1172
01:51:09,400 --> 01:51:13,359
Their fight is in the battlefield
and ours is here, girl.

1173
01:51:14,160 --> 01:51:19,399
Our fight is to keep our people
safe and cover our fears with faith.

1174
01:51:20,600 --> 01:51:24,639
My heart always hurts.

1175
01:51:25,440 --> 01:51:27,759
Not only for Osman and my children...

1176
01:51:27,880 --> 01:51:33,559
...but also for the raided village, the
world of Islam and all the innocent people.

1177
01:51:37,960 --> 01:51:39,959
You will get used to it.

1178
01:51:46,440 --> 01:51:49,119
Allah is Eternal!
Allah is The Righteous!

1179
01:51:51,400 --> 01:51:54,399
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

1180
01:52:12,640 --> 01:52:14,359
For my father!

1181
01:52:42,960 --> 01:52:45,039
Damn it.

1182
01:52:45,880 --> 01:52:47,759
Hristo!

1183
01:53:01,600 --> 01:53:04,079
My Bey, he's running off!

1184
01:53:09,280 --> 01:53:11,479
Osman

1185
01:53:11,760 --> 01:53:14,279
You won today, but tomorrow...

1186
01:53:14,680 --> 01:53:19,359
...I will take your heart
out and make wolves eat it!

1187
01:53:22,120 --> 01:53:24,679
Don't run away if you have courage, dastard!

1188
01:53:57,480 --> 01:54:00,399
Tie this rope somewhere solid, Hristo.

1189
01:54:00,400 --> 01:54:02,399
Will we leave Akhisar to Turks, commander Lukas?

1190
01:54:02,440 --> 01:54:04,879
The army of Nikea will never arrive, Hristo.

1191
01:54:05,240 --> 01:54:08,559
If we want to stop Osman's
advance, we have to live.

1192
01:54:08,560 --> 01:54:10,919
Tie the rope immediately.

1193
01:55:01,800 --> 01:55:03,679
He's out of range, my Bey.

1194
01:55:04,400 --> 01:55:07,719
He can't run away anymore.
He's going to die soon.

1195
01:55:10,880 --> 01:55:15,879
The castle of Akhisar belongs to Kayis now!

1196
01:55:16,000 --> 01:55:20,799
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!

1197
01:55:21,360 --> 01:55:24,599
Alps, don't you hear?

1198
01:55:24,880 --> 01:55:28,039
Raise the glorious banners of Kayi!

1199
01:55:28,120 --> 01:55:33,439
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!

1200
01:55:38,320 --> 01:55:40,719
Attention! Osman Bey!

1201
01:55:58,600 --> 01:56:03,959
This raid we started thinking that we
have campaigns and Allah offers victory...

1202
01:56:04,280 --> 01:56:05,959
...is crowned with a conquest.

1203
01:56:06,160 --> 01:56:11,799
Now this place will be enlightened
with the true religion Islam...

1204
01:56:12,480 --> 01:56:16,719
...and Akhisar will be reshaped
with the laws of Turks, God willing

1205
01:56:16,920 --> 01:56:20,199
This is the land of Turks now!

1206
01:56:20,440 --> 01:56:21,759
Allah is the greatest!

1207
01:56:21,840 --> 01:56:29,119
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!

1208
01:56:40,720 --> 01:56:42,999
My Bey, may your conquest be holy.

1209
01:56:43,200 --> 01:56:45,999
I've brought lots of regards
from the lands of Turks.

1210
01:56:46,160 --> 01:56:48,079
Peace be upon you too.

1211
01:56:48,440 --> 01:56:51,439
Thank you for that.
Samil.

1212
01:56:51,720 --> 01:56:53,679
You'll continue your duty.

1213
01:56:53,680 --> 01:56:55,999
You'll have the control of the frontiers.

1214
01:56:56,000 --> 01:56:57,839
Of course, my Bey.

1215
01:57:02,440 --> 01:57:04,719
May your conquest be holy, my Bey.

1216
01:57:04,840 --> 01:57:06,479
What's the matter, Alaaddin?

1217
01:57:06,880 --> 01:57:08,679
Is there a problem in the tribe?

1218
01:57:10,080 --> 01:57:11,359
My Bey.

1219
01:57:11,520 --> 01:57:14,959
The vile dog called Toyga

1220
01:57:15,840 --> 01:57:17,559
What about him?

1221
01:57:18,880 --> 01:57:21,479
He raided the tribes in the frontiers.

1222
01:57:21,800 --> 01:57:24,039
He burned down everything, my Bey.

1223
01:57:24,480 --> 01:57:26,359
Is that so?

1224
01:57:29,400 --> 01:57:32,599
I sent alps after him and warned everyone.

1225
01:57:32,960 --> 01:57:36,359
He was last seen in Demirbilek.

1226
01:57:37,120 --> 01:57:38,799
He is intimidating us, my Bey.

1227
01:57:39,200 --> 01:57:41,359
Trying to make us kneel.

1228
01:57:44,280 --> 01:57:46,879
If he has harmed people,

1229
01:57:47,160 --> 01:57:52,159
If even a single man has got hurt

1230
01:57:52,960 --> 01:57:55,719
...I will make their life miserable.

1231
01:57:56,920 --> 01:58:00,319
Get on horses! We will go make them pay

1232
01:58:11,000 --> 01:58:13,239
Osman

1233
01:58:17,840 --> 01:58:19,439
Damn it.

1234
01:58:19,800 --> 01:58:22,519
Damn it! Osman

1235
01:58:23,120 --> 01:58:25,279
I swear...

1236
01:58:25,600 --> 01:58:30,319
...I won't let you live
even at the cost of my life!

1237
01:58:33,200 --> 01:58:37,279
We'll make Osman face the most painful death.

1238
01:58:37,960 --> 01:58:40,079
Lukas.

1239
01:58:42,880 --> 01:58:46,719
I created such a trouble for Osman...

1240
01:58:52,200 --> 01:58:55,399
...that Mongolians won't let him take a break!

1241
01:58:59,400 --> 01:59:02,799
While Osman deal with Mongolians,

1242
01:59:04,560 --> 01:59:07,599
We will prepare his hell.

1243
01:59:07,920 --> 01:59:13,239
Everything he took from
us is going to destroy him.

1244
01:59:14,360 --> 01:59:15,919
Even a weapon.

1245
01:59:16,320 --> 01:59:18,959
Akhisar is just one of them.

1246
01:59:19,960 --> 01:59:26,879
And Osman won't realize anything
as he will have to deal with Mongolians.

1247
01:59:29,160 --> 01:59:32,999
Our victory is soon, Lukas.

1248
01:59:35,560 --> 01:59:39,359
We will take revenge.

1249
01:59:49,000 --> 01:59:52,279
You know Mongolians don't fight fairly, Sisters.

1250
01:59:52,760 --> 01:59:56,799
We should be prepared for any kind of fight.

1251
01:59:58,600 --> 02:00:01,239
Faster, stronger.

1252
02:00:12,080 --> 02:00:13,479
Meryem.

1253
02:00:15,080 --> 02:00:17,119
The threat of Mongolians is at the gate.

1254
02:00:17,200 --> 02:00:20,839
You need to learn how to protect
yourself as soon as possible.

1255
02:00:20,840 --> 02:00:24,119
You care about me so much
Fatma Hatun. Thank you.

1256
02:00:26,680 --> 02:00:28,119
You know what?

1257
02:00:29,520 --> 02:00:32,279
I also thought about this yesterday.

1258
02:00:32,880 --> 02:00:35,039
The moment I first saw you

1259
02:00:35,680 --> 02:00:37,879
..I felt close to you.

1260
02:00:38,400 --> 02:00:41,079
Maybe, you felt pity.

1261
02:00:41,200 --> 02:00:43,919
No. Not like that.

1262
02:00:47,720 --> 02:00:50,959
This is a feeling that I had
forgotten for a long time.

1263
02:00:57,880 --> 02:01:00,319
Whatever. Let's continue.

1264
02:01:12,880 --> 02:01:14,679
Come on, Meryem

1265
02:01:15,160 --> 02:01:16,999
Show your move.

1266
02:01:34,040 --> 02:01:36,359
That's it.

1267
02:01:37,920 --> 02:01:40,919
Come on, Meryem. Make your move.

1268
02:02:08,480 --> 02:02:10,719
No, no.

1269
02:02:13,080 --> 02:02:15,439
Check if there are any wounded men!

1270
02:02:15,720 --> 02:02:19,959
Mother, wake up... Mother...

1271
02:02:20,400 --> 02:02:23,039
How could you kill my innocent people?

1272
02:02:26,800 --> 02:02:28,519
How could you do this?

1273
02:02:29,160 --> 02:02:31,039
What did these people do to you?

1274
02:02:33,240 --> 02:02:35,359
What did these people do to you?

1275
02:02:38,400 --> 02:02:41,839
Mother wake up. Mother..

1276
02:02:42,080 --> 02:02:44,719
Come, my dear. Come.

1277
02:02:44,720 --> 02:02:47,879
Come. Come.

1278
02:02:51,330 --> 02:02:53,679
Come.. My dear.

1279
02:02:53,680 --> 02:02:57,199
They killed my mother, Osman
Bey. They burned our tribe down.

1280
02:02:57,200 --> 02:02:58,799
Why did they do this?

1281
02:02:58,800 --> 02:03:02,039
You will make them pay
for this, right, Osman Bey?

1282
02:03:07,120 --> 02:03:09,319
Don't worry.

1283
02:03:10,320 --> 02:03:14,519
Would I ever let them get away with this?

1284
02:03:15,280 --> 02:03:18,159
Would I? My dear...

1285
02:03:18,680 --> 02:03:21,439
Don't be afraid..
Don't be afraid..

1286
02:03:22,400 --> 02:03:25,639
Even if a thousand of them come...

1287
02:03:25,640 --> 02:03:30,559
...I will not let any of
them live on these lands.

1288
02:03:30,560 --> 02:03:33,239
I swear.

1289
02:03:33,840 --> 02:03:38,279
I swear.

1290
02:03:44,360 --> 02:03:46,519
Osman

1291
02:03:50,080 --> 02:03:52,719
I was looking for you

1292
02:04:09,600 --> 02:04:11,399
Boran.

1293
02:04:18,960 --> 02:04:20,879
You infidel...

1294
02:04:24,720 --> 02:04:27,039
I'm coming from the tribe down there.

1295
02:04:27,080 --> 02:04:28,639
You should go there as well.

1296
02:04:30,160 --> 02:04:32,439
You should see the strength of Mongols.

1297
02:04:40,480 --> 02:04:41,919
I will now...

1298
02:04:46,400 --> 02:04:50,279
You killed my people.

1299
02:04:51,400 --> 02:04:53,639
You killed my innocent people.

1300
02:04:54,840 --> 02:04:57,239
You killed my children.

1301
02:05:13,200 --> 02:05:15,359
Are you going to bring me to account?

1302
02:05:15,880 --> 02:05:18,799
Who are you to stand against the Mongol state

1303
02:05:20,960 --> 02:05:23,159
You cannot do anything to me.

1304
02:05:27,240 --> 02:05:28,519
I came here...

1305
02:05:28,600 --> 02:05:31,159
...as the envoy of the Mongol state.

1306
02:05:31,160 --> 02:05:32,959
And you gave your answer.

1307
02:05:35,200 --> 02:05:36,639
From now on...

1308
02:05:37,040 --> 02:05:38,519
...you are not facing...

1309
02:05:38,600 --> 02:05:42,279
...the envoy of the Mongol
state, but its Commander!

1310
02:05:47,080 --> 02:05:48,399
These heads..

1311
02:05:48,400 --> 02:05:50,519
...are the response to your answer.

1312
02:05:51,320 --> 02:05:56,199
If you do not kneel and
pledge allegiance, your sons...

1313
02:05:56,400 --> 02:06:02,039
...your Hatun, your daughter
will die the same way.

1314
02:06:03,920 --> 02:06:06,839
Kneel and pledge allegiance Osman!

1315
02:06:08,560 --> 02:06:14,559
Even if the whole world
collapses on me, I will only give...

1316
02:06:16,240 --> 02:06:19,759
...blood and bones to you

1317
02:06:38,280 --> 02:06:40,599
You are making a mistake Osman.

1318
02:06:44,920 --> 02:06:47,559
Who are you? Who?

1319
02:06:48,440 --> 02:06:49,639
Come here!

1320
02:06:50,040 --> 02:06:51,119
Come here!

1321
02:06:54,840 --> 02:06:57,039
Stand up! Stand up!

1322
02:07:12,960 --> 02:07:15,719
Your people will die, Osman

1323
02:07:16,200 --> 02:07:18,599
Your lands will turn into a bloodbath.

1324
02:07:20,080 --> 02:07:25,679
The dead in their graves... they will
dig up all their bones and burn them.

1325
02:07:28,480 --> 02:07:30,079
I swear...

1326
02:07:30,920 --> 02:07:32,439
I swear...

1327
02:07:32,920 --> 02:07:34,719
I and the ones behind me...

1328
02:07:35,800 --> 02:07:36,959
...until the sun..

1329
02:07:37,120 --> 02:07:38,999
...rises from the west...

1330
02:07:39,120 --> 02:07:41,679
...will always exist...

1331
02:07:41,760 --> 02:07:45,039
...for dogs like you

1332
02:07:45,040 --> 02:07:48,719
Dastard dog

1333
02:07:53,600 --> 02:07:56,519
You will see Osman...

1334
02:07:56,520 --> 02:08:00,119
You will see the strength of Mongols...

1335
02:08:00,120 --> 02:08:02,999
You will see the strength of Commander Ulugan.

1336
02:08:03,120 --> 02:08:05,159
But you won't be able to see it.

1337
02:08:05,360 --> 02:08:07,599
We always have valiants on these lands.

1338
02:08:07,920 --> 02:08:09,599
But those like you...

1339
02:08:10,240 --> 02:08:13,839
But those like you won't be
able to take a step on these lands.

1340
02:08:13,840 --> 02:08:16,559
Make him bow!

1341
02:08:32,360 --> 02:08:33,839
You cannot..

1342
02:08:34,480 --> 02:08:35,759
...stand against...

1343
02:08:36,440 --> 02:08:38,639
...Mongols, Osman.

1344
02:09:07,040 --> 02:09:10,119
I am not only standing against them...

1345
02:09:10,560 --> 02:09:12,959
I am also cutting their heads off!

1346
02:09:49,720 --> 02:09:51,799
We have fought with many enemies.

1347
02:09:52,440 --> 02:09:58,199
Thanks to my Allah, we always
gained a victory and defeated them.

1348
02:09:58,600 --> 02:10:00,319
But you should know.

1349
02:10:00,600 --> 02:10:04,239
Mongols have always been troublesome.

1350
02:10:05,760 --> 02:10:08,759
Thus, send word to everyone.

1351
02:10:08,760 --> 02:10:12,199
To all tribes, to all castles!

1352
02:10:12,520 --> 02:10:18,039
Now everyone should know, the
war of existence for Turks has begun

1353
02:10:18,680 --> 02:10:23,479
We will either be martyrs,
or we will exist forever!

1354
02:10:23,480 --> 02:10:25,119
Allah is the Greatest!

1355
02:10:25,880 --> 02:10:27,159
Allah is the Greatest!

1356
02:10:27,160 --> 02:10:30,519
Allah is the Greatest!
Allah is the Greatest!

1357
02:11:16,520 --> 02:11:18,159
Holy Commander Ulugan.

1358
02:11:19,600 --> 02:11:21,399
I gained Kayis' trust.

1359
02:11:22,400 --> 02:11:25,199
I became the most trustworthy Alp of Osman.

1360
02:11:35,600 --> 02:11:37,719
Osman cut Toygar's head off.

1361
02:11:39,160 --> 02:11:41,999
I am waiting for your order to make a move.

1362
02:11:52,200 --> 02:11:59,319
I am Osman Bey, of the
Oghuz Turks, from the Kayi tribe.

1363
02:12:00,080 --> 02:12:05,199
In these frontiers, where the few
have gained a victory over the many...

1364
02:12:05,440 --> 02:12:08,199
...I have never bowed to oppression.

1365
02:12:08,400 --> 02:12:10,039
Many became one against me...

1366
02:12:10,280 --> 02:12:11,839
...and they attacked me at once.

1367
02:12:12,240 --> 02:12:15,999
I fought without having a rest or giving up.

1368
02:12:16,760 --> 02:12:22,839
I am speaking to those who are worried
that jackals will get in the wolf's den.

1369
02:12:23,960 --> 02:12:27,759
Victory is ours, oppression is theirs.

1370
02:12:28,040 --> 02:12:30,279
Honor and shahada are for us.

1371
02:12:31,000 --> 02:12:34,839
Suffering and death are for them.